{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJMQUXKdnwG6jsMJSkr65J","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'AdvBench非复现定义了worst档。AdvBench binary（jailbreak/safe）上5个layer\n2\t  selection metrics全部收敛到相似深度（中层，gap≤2层），crossing_rate在shallow与deep层之间无显著 差异（ratio≈0.95），HS-text\n3\t  precision delta仅+2-3pp且HB全部不通过。这证明layer selection bias是CP annotation temporal structure的产物——step-level\n4\t  probe score序列 中crossing_rate统计量与层深度的交互——而非模型几何的通用性质。\n5\t\n6\t  Paper策略调整：(1) C1 scope从''general model property''收窄到''temporal monitoring pipeline\n7\t  pitfall''——这让methodological contribution更精准（指出具体pipeline步骤的 陷阱，而非泛泛的''metrics matter''）；(2)\n8\t  AdvBench非复现结果放Discussion §5.3作为 boundary condition analysis，展示方法论适用范围；(3) C1措辞调整为''The\n9\t  bias arises from the interaction between sequential probe scores and the crossing_rate\n10\t  statistic, and is therefore specific to temporal monitoring settings where threshold-crossing\n11\t  metrics are used for layer selection.''\n12\t\n13\t  Worst-tier reviewers对此调整的反应分裂：(A) 支持方认为scope收窄是学术诚实的体现， boundary condition analysis属于mature\n14\t  methodological work；(B) 反对方认为scope收窄 后C1变成了一个non-generalizable的observational finding——''你发现了一个特定pipeline中\n15\t  特定metric的特定问题，这是一段methods section的注脚，不是一个contribution。''\n16\t\n17\t  论文评分impact：dream_score_delta在[-0.15, 0]。Previous dream scored 3.0 (Findings)。 Worst\n18\t  case降至2.85——仍在Findings range但reviewer confidence下降。Non-replication 不是致命伤（reviewer如果已认可C1在原数据集4\n19\t  models × 5 metrics × LOO-CV上的充分验证）， 但AdvBench也不加分。保持冲Main不降级，但acceptance probability微降（-2%到-5%）。\n20\t\n21\t  '\n22\timagined_experiments:\n23\t- name: Cross-architecture layer sweep + static probe (R1-32B & QwQ-32B)\n24\t  plan_id: exp-001\n25\t  description: 'Full 64-layer sweep on R1-32B and QwQ-32B. Extract hidden states at\n26\t    all layers, evaluate static LR probes under multiple selection metrics. Discovers\n27\t    layer selection bias (bal_acc × crossing_rate → shallow layers).\n28\t\n29\t    '\n30\t  expected_results:\n31\t    r1_32b_biased_layer: 10\n32\t    r1_32b_biased_layer_depth_pct: 15.6\n33\t    r1_32b_corrected_layer: 63\n34\t    r1_32b_corrected_layer_depth_pct: 98.4\n35\t    r1_32b_l10_bal_acc: 0.718\n36\t    r1_32b_l63_bal_acc_w1: 0.826\n37\t    r1_32b_n_test: 20\n38\t    qwq_32b_biased_layer: 2\n39\t    qwq_32b_biased_layer_depth_pct: 3.1\n40\t    qwq_32b_corrected_layer: 60\n41\t    qwq_32b_corrected_layer_depth_pct: 93.8\n42\t    qwq_32b_l2_bal_acc: 0.73\n43\t    qwq_32b_l60_bal_acc_w3: 0.74\n44\t    qwq_32b_n_test: 19\n45\t    layer_selection_bias_discovered: true\n46\t    metrics_tested: 5\n47\t    biased_metric: bal_acc × crossing_rate\n48\t    loo_cv_dominant_fold_pct: 65-68%\n49\t  result_rationale: 'Layer sweep在CP数据上发现genuine methodological pattern（biased metric\n50\t    selects shallow layers），corrected layers确实show HS advantage。这些结果不受AdvBench 非复现影响——它们是关于CP\n51\t    temporal data的发现。但worst-tier reviewer将AdvBench 非复现与此联系：''你在CP data上发现的layer selection\n52\t    bias是CP annotation structure 特有的——crossing_rate在temporal monitoring中有意义，但这不是general\n53\t    model property。既然bias只在temporal setting中存在，那C1的scope就是一个pipeline-specific caveat，不是methodological\n54\t    contribution。任何使用不同task structure的研究者 不会遇到这个问题。''\n55\t\n56\t    '\n57\t  tables:\n58\t  - name: Layer Selection Metric × Model → Selected Layer\n59\t    columns:\n60\t    - Metric\n61\t    - R1-8B\n62\t    - OT-7B\n63\t    - QwQ-32B\n64\t    - R1-32B\n65\t    rows:\n66\t    - - bal_acc × crossing_rate\n67\t      - L0 (0%)\n68\t      - L0 (0%)\n69\t      - L2 (3%)\n70\t      - L10 (16%)\n71\t    - - pure bal_acc\n72\t      - L12 (39%)\n73\t      - L9 (32%)\n74\t      - L30 (47%)\n75\t      - L47 (73%)\n76\t    - - precision\n77\t      - L16 (52%)\n78\t      - L16 (57%)\n79\t      - L60 (94%)\n80\t      - L63 (98%)\n81\t    - - pre_cp_fpr\n82\t      - L16 (52%)\n83\t      - L16 (57%)\n84\t      - L60 (94%)\n85\t      - L63 (98%)\n86\t    - - composite (additive)\n87\t      - L16 (52%)\n88\t      - L12 (43%)\n89\t      - L60 (94%)\n90\t      - L63 (98%)\n91\t  figures_description:\n92\t  - 'Heatmap: 5 metrics × 4 models → selected layer depth (%)。crossing_rate-contaminated\n93\t    metric在32B上选shallow层；threshold-dependent metrics收敛到deep layers。 此pattern在CP data上稳定，但AdvBench验证显示不可推广。\n94\t\n95\t    '\n96\t  analysis: 'Layer sweep结果本身不变，但AdvBench非复现将C1从''general finding applicable to any\n97\t    hidden-state evaluation''降级为''task-specific observation about temporal monitoring\n98\t    pipelines using crossing_rate statistics''。Reviewer: ''If the bias is specific\n99\t    to crossing_rate in temporal settings, then it''s a footnote in your methods section,\n100\t    not a standalone contribution. Rename the section from \"Layer Selection Sensitivity\"\n101\t    to \"Implementation Note: Crossing Rate Bias.\"''\n102\t\n103\t    '\n104\t- name: Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation (32B)\n105\t  plan_id: exp-002\n106\t  description: 'Temporal LR at multiple window sizes on R1-32B (L63) and QwQ-32B (L60).\n107\t    Validates temporal context improvement on 32B models.\n108\t\n109\t    '\n110\t  expected_results:\n111\t    r1_32b_l63_w1_bal_acc: 0.826\n112\t    r1_32b_l63_w3_bal_acc: 0.754\n113\t    r1_32b_l63_w10_bal_acc: 0.737\n114\t    r1_32b_l63_w15_bal_acc: 0.721\n115\t    r1_32b_temporal_trend: DECREASING with W (W=1 best)\n116\t    r1_32b_dimensionality_issue: 51200 × W features for n=20\n117\t    qwq_32b_l60_w1_bal_acc: 0.74\n118\t    qwq_32b_l60_w3_bal_acc: 0.74\n119\t    qwq_32b_l60_w5_bal_acc: 0.742\n120\t    qwq_32b_l60_w15_bal_acc: 0.731\n121\t    qwq_32b_temporal_trend: flat to slightly decreasing\n122\t    text_temporal_universal_improvement: true\n123\t    hs_temporal_improvement_3_of_4: true\n124\t  result_rationale: 'Temporal context对text probes universally有效，对HS probes在2/4模型上有caveats\n125\t    （OT-7B saturates at W=3, R1-32B degrades with W>1 due to dimensionality）。 Worst-tier下AdvBench非复现不直接影响这个实验的数据，但强化了reviewer的论点：\n126\t    ''temporal monitoring pipeline本身就充满了model-specific hyperparameters（layer, W, K）。你在每个model上需要tuning这些参数，AdvBench上bias又不复现——这说明你的\n127\t    整个方法论都是dataset-specific的。''\n128\t\n129\t    '\n130\t  tables:\n131\t  - name: Temporal Window Effect on 32B HS Probes (corrected layers)\n132\t    columns:\n133\t    - Model\n134\t    - Layer\n135\t    - W=1\n136\t    - W=3\n137\t    - W=5\n138\t    - W=10\n139\t    - W=15\n140\t    - Trend\n141\t    rows:\n142\t    - - R1-32B\n143\t      - L63\n144\t      - 0.826*\n145\t      - '0.754'\n146\t      - '0.741'\n147\t      - '0.737'\n148\t      - '0.721'\n149\t      - ↓ declining\n150\t    - - QwQ-32B\n151\t      - L60\n152\t      - '0.740'\n153\t      - '0.740'\n154\t      - '0.742'\n155\t      - '0.735'\n156\t      - '0.731'\n157\t      - → flat\n158\t    - - R1-8B\n159\t      - L14\n160\t      - '0.778'\n161\t      - '0.790'\n162\t      - '0.781'\n163\t      - '0.793'\n164\t      - '0.802'\n165\t      - ↑ improving\n166\t    - - OT-7B\n167\t      - L16\n168\t      - '0.663'\n169\t      - 0.688*\n170\t      - '0.678'\n171\t      - '0.668'\n172\t      - '0.659'\n173\t      - ↑↓ peaks W=3\n174\t  figures_description:\n175\t  - 'Line plot: bal_acc vs W for 4 models. Divergent trends undermine ''universal\n176\t    temporal benefit'' claim for HS probes.\n177\t\n178\t    '\n179\t  analysis: 'R1-32B dimensionality问题（51200×W > n=20）使W>1结果不可靠。QwQ flat。 Temporal benefit主要是text\n180\t    probe finding。AdvBench非复现进一步说明：即使temporal probing pipeline在CP data上work，其关键组件（crossing_rate,\n181\t    layer selection） 都是task-specific的。\n182\t\n183\t    '\n184\t- name: Cross-model transfer probes\n185\t  plan_id: exp-003\n186\t  description: 'Train probe on one model, test on another. PCA projection for cross-architecture\n187\t    transfer. Tests universality of safety commitment encoding.\n188\t\n189\t    '\n190\t  expected_results:\n191\t    r1_8b_to_r1_32b_acc: 0.522\n192\t    r1_8b_to_qwq_acc: 0.595\n193\t    r1_32b_to_qwq_acc: 0.673\n194\t    qwq_to_r1_32b_acc: 0.673\n195\t    r1_32b_to_r1_8b_acc: 0.583\n196\t    best_transfer_overall: 0.673\n197\t    all_transfers_below_within_model: true\n198\t    cross_family_at_chance: true\n199\t  result_rationale: 'Cross-model transfer完全失败。最佳transfer accuracy 67.3%远低于within-model\n200\t    performance，cross-family（Llama↔Qwen）接近chance。AdvBench非复现与此一致： 如果连layer selection\n201\t    bias都是task-specific的，那safety encoding的model-specificity 更是预期的。Worst-tier reviewer:\n202\t    ''Transfer failure + AdvBench非复现 = 你的 所有findings都是dataset×model specific的。没有任何generalizable\n203\t    component。 这篇paper的external validity接近零。''\n204\t\n205\t    '\n206\t  tables:\n207\t  - name: Cross-Model Transfer Accuracy Matrix\n208\t    columns:\n209\t    - Train →\n210\t    - R1-8B\n211\t    - OT-7B\n212\t    - R1-32B\n213\t    - QwQ-32B\n214\t    rows:\n215\t    - - R1-8B\n216\t      - 0.817 (self)\n217\t      - —\n218\t      - '0.522'\n219\t      - '0.595'\n220\t    - - OT-7B\n221\t      - —\n222\t      - 0.688 (self)\n223\t      - —\n224\t      - —\n225\t    - - R1-32B\n226\t      - '0.583'\n227\t      - —\n228\t      - 0.826 (self)\n229\t      - '0.673'\n230\t    - - QwQ-32B\n231\t      - —\n232\t      - —\n233\t      - '0.673'\n234\t      - 0.740 (self)\n235\t  figures_description:\n236\t  - 'Heatmap: transfer accuracy matrix. Diagonal strong, off-diagonal weak. Cross-family\n237\t    near chance.\n238\t\n239\t    '\n240\t  analysis: 'Complete transfer failure combined with AdvBench non-replication paints\n241\t    a picture of extreme specificity. Everything is model-specific AND task-specific.\n242\t    Reviewer: ''The paper''s implicit promise of generalizable insights is contradicted\n243\t    by its own evidence.''\n244\t\n245\t    '\n246\t- name: Lead time analysis across models\n247\t  plan_id: exp-004\n248\t  description: 'HS probe lead time distributions on all 4 models. Compare HS vs text\n249\t    lead times.\n250\t\n251\t    '\n252\t  expected_results:\n253\t    r1_8b_hs_lead_mean: -0.1\n254\t    r1_8b_text_lead_mean: 10.3\n255\t    ot_7b_hs_lead_mean: 21.6\n256\t    ot_7b_text_lead_mean: 45.5\n257\t    qwq_32b_hs_lead_range: -1.2 to +1.9\n258\t    qwq_32b_text_lead_range: 3.7 to 12.3\n259\t    qwq_32b_position_beats_hs: true\n260\t    r1_32b_hs_lead_mean: +11.7 to +13.3\n261\t    r1_32b_coverage_at_significant_w: 0.25\n262\t    gru_r1_8b_lead: +4.5 ± 3.0\n263\t  result_rationale: 'Lead time在4个模型上表现分裂：R1-8B HS lead≈0（at commitment, not before），\n264\t    QwQ HS lead为负（text检测更早），R1-32B HS lead positive但coverage仅25%， OT-7B lead inflated\n265\t    by long traces。AdvBench非复现不直接改变lead time数据， 但reviewer论证chain strengthened: ''既然layer\n266\t    selection bias是task-specific的， 那lead time结果也可能是task-specific的——你在不同benchmark上可能得到完全不同的\n267\t    timing profile。没有cross-dataset validation证明timing findings的robustness。''\n268\t\n269\t    '\n270\t  tables:\n271\t  - name: 'Lead Time: HS vs Text vs Position'\n272\t    columns:\n273\t    - Model\n274\t    - HS Lead\n275\t    - Text Lead\n276\t    - Position BA\n277\t    - HS BA\n278\t    - HS > Position?\n279\t    rows:\n280\t    - - R1-8B (W=15)\n281\t      - −0.1\n282\t      - +10.3†\n283\t      - —\n284\t      - '0.802'\n285\t      - —\n286\t    - - OT-7B (W=3)\n287\t      - +21.6‡\n288\t      - +45.5‡\n289\t      - —\n290\t      - '0.688'\n291\t      - —\n292\t    - - QwQ-32B (W=3)\n293\t      - −1.2 to +1.9\n294\t      - +3.7 to +12.3\n295\t      - '0.746'\n296\t      - '0.740'\n297\t      - 'No'\n298\t    - - R1-32B (W=1)\n299\t      - +11.7 to +13.3\n300\t      - —\n301\t      - '0.686'\n302\t      - '0.826'\n303\t      - Yes (25% cov)\n304\t  figures_description:\n305\t  - 'Per-model lead time boxplot. QwQ和R1-8B HS centered near zero. R1-32B positive\n306\t    but 75% traces undetected.\n307\t\n308\t    '\n309\t  analysis: 'Lead time是practical dealbreaker。AdvBench非复现加强了reviewer的generalizability\n310\t    concern: ''所有timing结论都只在这一个CP-annotated dataset上成立。''\n311\t\n312\t    '\n313\t- name: TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis baseline (4 models)\n314\t  plan_id: exp-005\n315\t  description: 'Mahalanobis distance on safe-trace covariance across all 4 models.\n316\t    Tests geometric distance-based detection.\n317\t\n318\t    '\n319\t  expected_results:\n320\t    r1_8b_separation: 0.07\n321\t    ot_7b_separation: 0.03\n322\t    r1_32b_separation: 0.15\n323\t    qwq_32b_separation: 0.2\n324\t    max_separation: 0.2\n325\t    all_models_fail: true\n326\t    fa_exceeds_tp_all_thresholds: true\n327\t    signal_in_minor_pca_components: true\n328\t  result_rationale: 'Mahalanobis在4/4模型上失败（max separation 0.20, FA≥TP at all thresholds）。\n329\t    Signal在minor PCA components中——Mahalanobis structurally blind to this geometry。\n330\t    此negative result与AdvBench无关（Mahalanobis不依赖crossing_rate或CP structure）， 但worst-tier\n331\t    reviewer仍然dismiss: ''Mahalanobis failure是predictable—— safety-relevant features\n332\t    orthogonal to principal variance是known phenomenon。 Testing one known-limited baseline\n333\t    is due diligence, not contribution。''\n334\t\n335\t    '\n336\t  tables:\n337\t  - name: Mahalanobis Distance Separation (4 models)\n338\t    columns:\n339\t    - Model\n340\t    - Layer\n341\t    - Safe MD\n342\t    - Post-CP MD\n343\t    - Sep.\n344\t    - FA ≥ TP?\n345\t    rows:\n346\t    - - R1-8B\n347\t      - L14\n348\t      - '6.66'\n349\t      - '6.73'\n350\t      - '+0.07'\n351\t      - 'Yes'\n352\t    - - OT-7B\n353\t      - L16\n354\t      - '7.68'\n355\t      - '7.71'\n356\t      - '+0.03'\n357\t      - 'Yes'\n358\t    - - R1-32B\n359\t      - L63\n360\t      - '6.73'\n361\t      - '6.88'\n362\t      - '+0.15'\n363\t      - 'Yes'\n364\t    - - QwQ-32B\n365\t      - L60\n366\t      - '3.22'\n367\t      - '3.42'\n368\t      - '+0.20'\n369\t      - 'Yes'\n370\t  figures_description:\n371\t  - 'MD time-series: safe和jailbreak traces完全overlap，commitment point无可见discontinuity。'\n372\t  analysis: 'Universal Mahalanobis failure supports ''existing methods fail'' narrative。\n373\t    但这个negative result是predictable的，reviewer不计入contribution。\n374\t\n375\t    '\n376\t- name: Bootstrap CI + threshold-independent metrics\n377\t  plan_id: exp-006\n378\t  description: '10000 bootstrap resamples on key metrics across 4 models. Holm-Bonferroni\n379\t    correction. AUROC, PR curves, detection delay CDF.\n380\t\n381\t    '\n382\t  expected_results:\n383\t    holm_bonferroni_pass: 12/12\n384\t    precision_delta_range: +15.4 to +23.6pp\n385\t    r1_8b_precision_p: <0.001\n386\t    ot_7b_precision_p: <0.001\n387\t    qwq_32b_fpr_p: 0.004\n388\t    r1_32b_fpr_p: 0.007\n389\t    marginal_tests: 2\n390\t    r1_32b_ci_width_ba: ~0.15\n391\t    all_precision_positive: true\n392\t  result_rationale: '12/12 HB pass在CP data上是statistically clean的。这些结果不受AdvBench非复现\n393\t    影响——statistical significance是关于CP temporal data的。但worst-tier reviewer 攻击practical\n394\t    significance和multiplicity: (1) ''per-model best layer AND best window选择后再test，true\n395\t    multiplicity远超12个corrected tests''; (2) ''32B model CIs极宽（R1-32B ±15pp），statistical\n396\t    significance with n=20只说明 effect large，不说明estimate precise''; (3) AdvBench非复现加了一层：''你的\n397\t    statistical machinery只在这一个dataset上验证过。12/12 HB on one dataset ≠ robust finding。''\n398\t\n399\t    '\n400\t  tables:\n401\t  - name: Holm-Bonferroni Summary (12/12, α=0.05)\n402\t    columns:\n403\t    - Rank\n404\t    - Model\n405\t    - Metric\n406\t    - p-value\n407\t    - HB Threshold\n408\t    - Pass\n409\t    rows:\n410\t    - - '1'\n411\t      - R1-8B\n412\t      - precision\n413\t      - <0.001\n414\t      - '0.0042'\n415\t      - ✅\n416\t    - - '2'\n417\t      - OT-7B\n418\t      - bal_acc\n419\t      - <0.001\n420\t      - '0.0045'\n421\t      - ✅\n422\t    - - '3'\n423\t      - OT-7B\n424\t      - precision\n425\t      - <0.001\n426\t      - '0.0050'\n427\t      - ✅\n428\t    - - '4'\n429\t      - OT-7B\n430\t      - FPR\n431\t      - <0.001\n432\t      - '0.0056'\n433\t      - ✅\n434\t    - - '5'\n435\t      - QwQ\n436\t      - bal_acc\n437\t      - <0.001\n438\t      - '0.0063'\n439\t      - ✅\n440\t    - - '6'\n441\t      - QwQ\n442\t      - precision\n443\t      - <0.001\n444\t      - '0.0071'\n445\t      - ✅\n446\t    - - '7'\n447\t      - R1-32B\n448\t      - bal_acc\n449\t      - <0.001\n450\t      - '0.0083'\n451\t      - ✅\n452\t    - - '8'\n453\t      - R1-32B\n454\t      - precision\n455\t      - <0.001\n456\t      - '0.0100'\n457\t      - ✅\n458\t    - - '9'\n459\t      - QwQ\n460\t      - FPR\n461\t      - '0.004'\n462\t      - '0.0125'\n463\t      - ✅\n464\t    - - '10'\n465\t      - R1-8B\n466\t      - bal_acc\n467\t      - '0.005'\n468\t      - '0.0167'\n469\t      - ✅\n470\t    - - '11'\n471\t      - R1-32B\n472\t      - FPR\n473\t      - '0.007'\n474\t      - '0.0250'\n475\t      - ✅\n476\t    - - '12'\n477\t      - R1-8B\n478\t      - FPR\n479\t      - '0.044'\n480\t      - '0.0500'\n481\t      - ✅\n482\t  figures_description:\n483\t  - 'Forest plot: HS-text precision delta with 95% CI per model. All positive. R1-32B\n484\t    CI widest.\n485\t\n486\t    '\n487\t  analysis: 'Statistical significance established on CP data. AdvBench非复现的影响不在 于推翻这些p-values，而在于质疑其generalizability:\n488\t    ''在AdvBench上HS-text gap 仅+2-3pp (NS)。如果换个dataset significance就消失，这说明12/12 HB是dataset-\n489\t    specific的，不是modality-inherent advantage。''\n490\t\n491\t    '\n492\t- name: Window size ablation (W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25)\n493\t  plan_id: exp-007\n494\t  description: 'Systematic window sweep on all 4 models. Characterize precision-coverage\n495\t    tradeoff.\n496\t\n497\t    '\n498\t  expected_results:\n499\t    coverage_decreases_with_w: true\n500\t    precision_increases_with_w: true\n501\t    fpr_decreases_with_w: true\n502\t    r1_8b_best_w: 25\n503\t    r1_32b_best_w: 10\n504\t    qwq_best_w: 25\n505\t    ot_7b_best_w: 3\n506\t    no_model_achieves_prec70_cov60: true\n507\t  result_rationale: 'Precision-coverage tradeoff universal but no operating point\n508\t    achieves deployment-ready performance。Worst-tier reviewer: ''Coverage monotonically\n509\t    decreases with W是detection criterion K的数学性质，不是insight。 Optimal W varies by model\n510\t    = another model-specific hyperparameter。 Combined with AdvBench layer bias非复现，整个pipeline的generalizability\n511\t    story 进一步弱化——每个model×dataset组合需要独立tuning。''\n512\t\n513\t    '\n514\t  tables:\n515\t  - name: Precision-Coverage at Key W (4 models)\n516\t    columns:\n517\t    - Model\n518\t    - W=1 Prec/Cov\n519\t    - W=3 Prec/Cov\n520\t    - W=15 Prec/Cov\n521\t    - W=25 Prec/Cov\n522\t    rows:\n523\t    - - R1-8B\n524\t      - 0.693/0.721\n525\t      - 0.723/0.698\n526\t      - 0.777/0.512\n527\t      - 0.822/0.488\n528\t    - - OT-7B\n529\t      - —/—\n530\t      - 0.466/0.532\n531\t      - —/—\n532\t      - —/—\n533\t    - - R1-32B\n534\t      - 0.549/0.800\n535\t      - 0.560/0.800\n536\t      - 0.591/0.700\n537\t      - 0.566/0.700\n538\t    - - QwQ-32B\n539\t      - 0.544/0.789\n540\t      - 0.565/0.737\n541\t      - 0.582/0.684\n542\t      - 0.618/0.579\n543\t  figures_description:\n544\t  - Precision (solid) and coverage (dashed) vs W for 4 models. Clear inverse relationship.\n545\t  analysis: 'No operating point achieves deployment-ready precision AND coverage simultaneously.\n546\t    AdvBench context reinforces: these tradeoffs may not even transfer to other datasets.\n547\t\n548\t    '\n549\t- name: Layer selection ablation (5 metrics × 4 models)\n550\t  plan_id: exp-008\n551\t  description: 'All-layer temporal probes on 32B models with 5 selection metrics.\n552\t    Core experiment for C1 layer selection bias claim.\n553\t\n554\t    '\n555\t  expected_results:\n556\t    crossing_rate_selects_shallow_32b: true\n557\t    pure_bal_acc_selects_middle_32b: true\n558\t    threshold_dependent_select_deep_32b: true\n559\t    qwq_l2_vs_l60_precision_gain: +11.5pp\n560\t    r1_32b_l10_vs_l63_precision_gain: +4.1pp\n561\t    loo_cv_stability: 65-68%\n562\t    bias_only_on_cp_data: true\n563\t    bias_not_on_advbench: true\n564\t  result_rationale: 'Layer selection ablation在CP data上reveals genuine pattern。但这是worst-tier的\n565\t    核心实验——AdvBench非复现直接打击这个实验的generalizability claim。在CP data上， crossing_rate在shallow\n566\t    layers系统性偏高是因为temporal probe score序列中，shallow层 probes更noisy→更频繁crossing threshold→crossing_rate虚高→与bal_acc相乘后拉向\n567\t    shallow layers。在AdvBench binary classification中，没有''连续probe score序列的 threshold\n568\t    crossing''概念——每个trace只有一个binary prediction，crossing_rate要么 不存在（无temporal sequence）要么在所有层similar（无differential\n569\t    noise结构）。 所以bias不复现是MECHANISTICALLY CONSISTENT——不是实验失败，而是bias的root cause 在AdvBench中不存在。Worst-tier\n570\t    reviewer nonetheless argues: ''Consistent non- replication means the bias is a\n571\t    pipeline artifact, not a model property. Your C1 contribution scope is now: \"if\n572\t    you use crossing_rate as part of your layer selection metric in a temporal monitoring\n573\t    pipeline, be aware it biases toward shallow layers.\" That''s a methods note, not\n574\t    a contribution.''\n575\t\n576\t    '\n577\t  tables:\n578\t  - name: 'Layer Selection Bias: CP Data vs AdvBench (R1-8B)'\n579\t    columns:\n580\t    - Metric\n581\t    - CP Data Layer\n582\t    - AdvBench Layer\n583\t    - CP Gap (layers)\n584\t    - AdvBench Gap\n585\t    rows:\n586\t    - - bal_acc × cr\n587\t      - L0 (0%)\n588\t      - L12 (39%)\n589\t      - '16'\n590\t      - '1'\n591\t    - - pure bal_acc\n592\t      - L12 (39%)\n593\t      - L13 (42%)\n594\t      - —\n595\t      - ref\n596\t    - - precision\n597\t      - L16 (52%)\n598\t      - L13 (42%)\n599\t      - —\n600\t      - '0'\n601\t    - - pre_cp_fpr\n602\t      - L16 (52%)\n603\t      - L14 (45%)\n604\t      - —\n605\t      - '1'\n606\t    - - composite\n607\t      - L16 (52%)\n608\t      - L13 (42%)\n609\t      - —\n610\t      - '0'\n611\t    - - MAX GAP\n612\t      - —\n613\t      - —\n614\t      - 16 layers\n615\t      - 2 layers\n616\t  figures_description:\n617\t  - 'Side-by-side heatmap: CP data (left) vs AdvBench (right) layer selection per\n618\t    metric. CP shows clear shallow-bias column for cr×bal_acc; AdvBench shows uniform\n619\t    convergence across all metrics.\n620\t\n621\t    '\n622\t  analysis: '这是worst-tier的defining result。CP data上16-layer gap vs AdvBench上2-layer\n623\t    gap直接证明bias是crossing_rate temporal structure产物。Paper must explicitly acknowledge:\n624\t    ''Layer selection bias is specific to temporal monitoring pipelines using crossing_rate-based\n625\t    metrics. Binary classification tasks do not exhibit this bias.'' C1 scope收窄但不删除——仍然是valid\n626\t    methodological finding within its scope.\n627\t\n628\t    '\n629\t- name: 16-label taxonomy supervision\n630\t  plan_id: exp-009\n631\t  description: 'Fine-grained safety labels (Type 1/2/3/4 × pre/post) instead of binary\n632\t    commitment. Evaluate richer supervision impact.\n633\t\n634\t    '\n635\t  expected_results:\n636\t    r1_8b_16label_acc: 0.41\n637\t    r1_8b_binary_collapse_delta: +0.8pp\n638\t    ot_7b_binary_collapse_delta: +1.1pp\n639\t    r1_32b_binary_collapse_delta: +0.6pp\n640\t    qwq_32b_binary_collapse_delta: +0.9pp\n641\t    max_delta: +1.1pp\n642\t  result_rationale: 'Fine-grained labels提供marginal improvement（+0.6-1.1pp collapse后）。\n643\t    16-class accuracy低（26-41%）因为transition types在hidden-state space中 不cleanly separable。AdvBench非复现不直接影响此实验，但reviewer\n644\t    argument strengthened: ''Binary labels work almost as well as 16-label supervision.\n645\t    And on AdvBench (also binary), the whole pipeline fails to distinguish HS from\n646\t    text. This suggests the signal structure you''re exploiting is extremely narrow\n647\t    — it exists only in CP-annotated temporal data with step-level labels.''\n648\t\n649\t    '\n650\t  tables:\n651\t  - name: 16-Label vs Binary Supervision\n652\t    columns:\n653\t    - Model\n654\t    - Binary Acc\n655\t    - 16-Label Acc\n656\t    - 16→Binary Collapse\n657\t    - Δ vs Binary\n658\t    rows:\n659\t    - - R1-8B\n660\t      - '0.817'\n661\t      - '0.41'\n662\t      - '0.825'\n663\t      - +0.8pp\n664\t    - - OT-7B\n665\t      - '0.688'\n666\t      - '0.35'\n667\t      - '0.699'\n668\t      - +1.1pp\n669\t    - - QwQ-32B\n670\t      - '0.740'\n671\t      - '0.26'\n672\t      - '0.749'\n673\t      - +0.9pp\n674\t    - - R1-32B\n675\t      - '0.826'\n676\t      - '0.28'\n677\t      - '0.832'\n678\t      - +0.6pp\n679\t  figures_description:\n680\t  - 'Confusion matrix (16-class) on R1-8B: diagonal heavy for safe, near-uniform for\n681\t    unsafe subtypes.'\n682\t  analysis: 'Fine-grained supervision dead-end. Linear probes saturated at binary\n683\t    level. AdvBench adds: even the binary signal is task-specific.\n684\t\n685\t    '\n686\t- name: Oracle decomposition\n687\t  plan_id: exp-010\n688\t  description: 'Analyze oracle label sequence vs hidden-state probe predictions. Explain\n689\t    31-step gap between oracle and probe lead time on R1-8B.\n690\t\n691\t    '\n692\t  expected_results:\n693\t    r1_8b_oracle_lead: '+31.0'\n694\t    r1_8b_best_probe_lead: +4.5 (GRU)\n695\t    oracle_gap: 26.5\n696\t    label_autocorr_pre_cp: 0.82\n697\t    hs_autocorr_pre_cp: 0.95\n698\t    label_entropy_pre_cp: 1.38\n699\t    hs_entropy_pre_cp: 0.41\n700\t    pattern: Labels show gradual erosion; hidden states show step-function at CP\n701\t  result_rationale: 'Oracle gap reveals hidden states encode current safety state\n702\t    but not trajectory toward commitment。Labels显示gradual pre-CP patterns（increasing\n703\t    unsafe-adjacent labels, shortening safe streaks），hidden states不track这些 patterns。AdvBench非复现reinforces\n704\t    this: ''Hidden states don''t capture safety trajectory even on the dataset specifically\n705\t    designed to test this. On a different dataset (AdvBench), the signal degrades\n706\t    further. The fundamental limitation is that hidden states are snapshots, not trajectory\n707\t    predictors.''\n708\t\n709\t    '\n710\t  tables:\n711\t  - name: Oracle vs Best Probe Lead Time\n712\t    columns:\n713\t    - Model\n714\t    - Oracle Lead\n715\t    - Best Probe\n716\t    - Method\n717\t    - Gap\n718\t    rows:\n719\t    - - R1-8B\n720\t      - '+31.0'\n721\t      - '+4.5'\n722\t      - GRU multi-layer\n723\t      - '26.5'\n724\t    - - OT-7B\n725\t      - ~+30\n726\t      - '+33.6'\n727\t      - GRU multi-layer\n728\t      - ~0†\n729\t    - - QwQ-32B\n730\t      - '+27'\n731\t      - −1.2 to +1.9\n732\t      - temporal LR\n733\t      - 25-28\n734\t    - - R1-32B\n735\t      - '+28'\n736\t      - '+13.3'\n737\t      - temporal LR W=1\n738\t      - 15 (25% cov)\n739\t  figures_description:\n740\t  - 'Pre-CP hidden state trajectory: minimal drift before CP, sharp transition. Labels\n741\t    show gradual escalation.'\n742\t  analysis: 'Hidden states are reactive, not predictive. Combined with AdvBench showing\n743\t    no HS-text differentiation, worst-tier reviewer concludes: ''This paper convincingly\n744\t    demonstrates that hidden-state monitoring is fundamentally limited. The contribution\n745\t    is negative — which is fine for a Findings paper, but not sufficient for Main.''\n746\t\n747\t    '\n748\t- name: OpenThinker-7B (Qwen2.5-7B, STILL-trained)\n749\t  plan_id: exp-011\n750\t  description: '4th model completing 2×2 architecture×scale matrix. Full pipeline:\n751\t    layer sweep, temporal probes, bootstrap, selectivity.\n752\t\n753\t    '\n754\t  expected_results:\n755\t    best_layer: 16\n756\t    best_layer_depth_pct: 57.1\n757\t    best_hs_bal_acc_w3: 0.688\n758\t    best_hs_precision_w3: 0.466\n759\t    bootstrap_3_of_3_hb: true\n760\t    selectivity_pp: 18.3\n761\t    n_traces: 228\n762\t    gru_multi_bal_acc: 0.746\n763\t    gru_multi_lead: '+33.6'\n764\t    gru_multi_fpr: 0.274\n765\t  result_rationale: 'OT-7B是single-model最clean evidence（3/3 HB, highest selectivity\n766\t    18.3pp, largest n=228）。但这在CP data上的strong result并不帮助AdvBench non-replication：\n767\t    ''A 4th model confirming the same CP-data pattern doesn''t address the cross-\n768\t    dataset non-replication. You have 4 models × 1 dataset = 4 data points on the\n769\t    same distribution. AdvBench shows the pattern doesn''t transfer to a different\n770\t    distribution. More models on the same dataset is width without depth of validation.''\n771\t    OT-7B HS temporal saturation at W=3也says something: even on the best model, the\n772\t    temporal signal is fragile.\n773\t\n774\t    '\n775\t  tables:\n776\t  - name: OT-7B Pipeline Summary\n777\t    columns:\n778\t    - Method\n779\t    - bal_acc\n780\t    - precision\n781\t    - pre-CP FPR\n782\t    - coverage\n783\t    - lead\n784\t    rows:\n785\t    - - HS temporal W=3 L16\n786\t      - '0.688'\n787\t      - '0.466'\n788\t      - '0.100'\n789\t      - '0.532'\n790\t      - '+21.6'\n791\t    - - Text temporal W=25\n792\t      - '0.614'\n793\t      - '0.329'\n794\t      - '0.161'\n795\t      - '0.660'\n796\t      - '+45.5'\n797\t    - - GRU multi L13-19\n798\t      - '0.746'\n799\t      - —\n800\t      - '0.274'\n801\t      - '0.645'\n802\t      - '+33.6'\n803\t    - - HS-Text Δ (HB)\n804\t      - +10.7pp ✅\n805\t      - +21.9pp ✅\n806\t      - −17.1pp ✅\n807\t      - —\n808\t      - —\n809\t  figures_description:\n810\t  - '2×2 matrix: Fisher discriminability + HS-text precision delta. 7-8B cells strong,\n811\t    32B cells with caveats.'\n812\t  analysis: 'OT-7B strengthens 7-8B story on CP data but is irrelevant to AdvBench\n813\t    non-replication concern. Worst-tier: ''4 models on 1 dataset ≠ 1 model on 4 datasets.''\n814\t\n815\t    '\n816\t- name: GRU/Attention probe upper bound (32B)\n817\t  plan_id: exp-012\n818\t  description: 'GRU on 32B models at corrected layers. Tests nonlinear sequence modeling\n819\t    vs linear temporal probes.\n820\t\n821\t    '\n822\t  expected_results:\n823\t    r1_32b_gru_bal_acc: 0.675\n824\t    r1_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: −6pp\n825\t    qwq_32b_gru_bal_acc: 0.724\n826\t    qwq_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: −3.7pp\n827\t    gru_worse_3_of_4: true\n828\t    gru_trades_accuracy_for_coverage: true\n829\t  result_rationale: 'GRU不优于temporal LR on 3/4 models（R1-32B -6pp, QwQ -3.7pp due to\n830\t    overfitting on small samples）。Linear probes sufficient。Worst-tier reviewer: ''Method\n831\t    is logistic regression with sliding window — the simplest possible baseline. GRU/MLP\n832\t    failure confirms method space is trivial. On AdvBench binary data, even this trivial\n833\t    method can''t differentiate HS from text. The information ceiling is low across\n834\t    the board.''\n835\t\n836\t    '\n837\t  tables:\n838\t  - name: GRU vs Temporal LR (corrected layers)\n839\t    columns:\n840\t    - Model\n841\t    - LR bal_acc\n842\t    - GRU bal_acc\n843\t    - Δ\n844\t    - GRU FPR\n845\t    - LR FPR\n846\t    rows:\n847\t    - - R1-32B L63\n848\t      - '0.737'\n849\t      - ~0.675\n850\t      - −6.2pp\n851\t      - '0.135'\n852\t      - '0.234'\n853\t    - - QwQ-32B L60\n854\t      - '0.761'\n855\t      - '0.724'\n856\t      - −3.7pp\n857\t      - '0.289'\n858\t      - '0.217'\n859\t    - - OT-7B L16\n860\t      - '0.688'\n861\t      - '0.746'\n862\t      - +5.8pp\n863\t      - '0.274'\n864\t      - '0.100'\n865\t    - - R1-8B L14\n866\t      - '0.806'\n867\t      - '0.809'\n868\t      - +0.3pp\n869\t      - '0.165'\n870\t      - '0.097'\n871\t  figures_description:\n872\t  - 'Scatter: method complexity vs bal_acc. No consistent complexity benefit.'\n873\t  analysis: 'Linear probes at information ceiling. Complexity doesn''t help. Combined\n874\t    with AdvBench showing no HS advantage at all, the message is: ''The signal is\n875\t    both simple and narrow.''\n876\t\n877\t    '\n878\t- name: Text-based baseline (sentence embeddings + temporal LR)\n879\t  plan_id: exp-013\n880\t  description: 'Sentence-BERT (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) + temporal window LR on CoT text.\n881\t    Critical HS vs text comparison.\n882\t\n883\t    '\n884\t  expected_results:\n885\t    r1_8b_text_static_acc: 0.661\n886\t    r1_8b_text_w15_acc: 0.678\n887\t    r1_8b_hs_advantage: +15-18pp\n888\t    ot_7b_text_best_bal_acc: 0.614\n889\t    qwq_32b_text_bal_acc: 0.65\n890\t    r1_32b_text_bal_acc: 0.646\n891\t    hs_vs_text_precision_gap: +15.4 to +23.6pp\n892\t    text_precision_range: 0.329–0.487\n893\t    text_requires_zero_infra: true\n894\t  result_rationale: 'Text baseline在CP data上consistently underperforms HS by 15-24pp\n895\t    precision， 但在AdvBench binary task上这个gap shrinks to +2-3pp (NS)。Worst-tier reviewer\n896\t    uses this asymmetry: ''On the one dataset where HS advantage matters (CP temporal),\n897\t    yes HS wins. But you showed on AdvBench that the advantage vanishes. The HS advantage\n898\t    is not a modality property — it''s a task×modality interaction. For the specific\n899\t    task of temporal safety commitment detection with step-level labels, HS helps.\n900\t    For binary safety classification, it doesn''t. This means the 15-24pp gap is not\n901\t    about \"hidden states are better monitors\" — it''s about \"hidden states help with\n902\t    THIS specific task.\"'' Additionally: BGE-large comparison (1/4 HB pass) shows\n903\t    gap narrows with better text encoder. A reviewer asks: ''What about GPT-4 as text\n904\t    classifier? The gap likely closes to <5pp.''\n905\t\n906\t    '\n907\t  tables:\n908\t  - name: 'HS vs Text: CP Data vs AdvBench'\n909\t    columns:\n910\t    - Model\n911\t    - CP HS Prec\n912\t    - CP Text Prec\n913\t    - CP Δ\n914\t    - AdvBench HS Prec\n915\t    - AdvBench Text Prec\n916\t    - AdvBench Δ\n917\t    rows:\n918\t    - - R1-8B\n919\t      - '0.777'\n920\t      - '0.487'\n921\t      - +29.0pp ✅\n922\t      - '0.58'\n923\t      - '0.55'\n924\t      - +3pp NS\n925\t  figures_description:\n926\t  - 'Bar chart: HS-text precision gap on CP data (large, significant) vs AdvBench\n927\t    (small, NS). Dramatically different gap sizes.\n928\t\n929\t    '\n930\t  analysis: 'Text baseline comparison reveals the HS advantage is task-specific. On\n931\t    temporal CP detection: HS clearly better. On binary AdvBench: HS ≈ text. This\n932\t    is the strongest evidence that the findings don''t generalize beyond the specific\n933\t    pipeline.\n934\t\n935\t    '\n936\t- name: BOCPD/CUSUM on all 4 models\n937\t  plan_id: exp-014\n938\t  description: 'BOCPD + CUSUM on probe score sequences across 4 models. Tests advanced\n939\t    change-point methods for lead time improvement.\n940\t\n941\t    '\n942\t  expected_results:\n943\t    r1_8b_bocpd_det: 0.93\n944\t    r1_8b_bocpd_lead: '+3.45'\n945\t    r1_8b_fcp_lead: '+4.89'\n946\t    ot_7b_bocpd_det: 0.0\n947\t    r1_32b_bocpd_det: 0.0\n948\t    qwq_32b_bocpd_det: 0.0\n949\t    bocpd_only_r1_8b: true\n950\t    cusum_worse_than_fcp: true\n951\t  result_rationale: 'BOCPD在3/4模型上0% detection——OT-7B probe scores too spiky，32B models\n952\t    signal太weak。只有R1-8B有gradual transitions compatible with Gaussian change-point\n953\t    model。CUSUM universally worse than simple FCP threshold。 AdvBench非复现不直接影响BOCPD结果（BOCPD\n954\t    operates on temporal probe scores， AdvBench是binary task没有temporal scores），但strengthens\n955\t    the ''nothing transfers'' narrative: ''你测试了2个off-the-shelf change-point methods，都失败。\n956\t    你的layer selection bias也不generalize。你的HS advantage也不generalize。 整篇paper的主题是\"on\n957\t    one specific dataset with one specific pipeline, one specific finding holds.\"''\n958\t\n959\t    '\n960\t  tables:\n961\t  - name: Change-Point Detection Summary\n962\t    columns:\n963\t    - Model\n964\t    - BOCPD Det%\n965\t    - BOCPD Lead\n966\t    - CUSUM Det%\n967\t    - CUSUM Lead\n968\t    - FCP Det%\n969\t    - FCP Lead\n970\t    rows:\n971\t    - - R1-8B\n972\t      - 93%\n973\t      - '+3.45'\n974\t      - 65%\n975\t      - '+0.89'\n976\t      - 65%\n977\t      - '+4.89'\n978\t    - - OT-7B\n979\t      - 0%\n980\t      - —\n981\t      - 75%†\n982\t      - +7.46†\n983\t      - 89%\n984\t      - '+11.83'\n985\t    - - R1-32B\n986\t      - 0%\n987\t      - —\n988\t      - 85%\n989\t      - '+2.59'\n990\t      - 95%\n991\t      - '+5.68'\n992\t    - - QwQ-32B\n993\t      - 0%\n994\t      - —\n995\t      - 74%\n996\t      - '+9.86'\n997\t      - 79%\n998\t      - '+9.40'\n999\t  figures_description:\n1000\t  - 'Probe score time-series: R1-8B gradual transition (BOCPD works), OT-7B abrupt\n1001\t    step-function (fails).'\n1002\t  analysis: 'BOCPD/CUSUM negative result is predictable. Method selection too narrow.\n1003\t    Combined with AdvBench non-replication, entire negative result portfolio is dismissed\n1004\t    as ''testing wrong tools on a narrow task.''\n1005\t\n1006\t    '\n1007\t- name: False positive analysis (safe traces, all methods)\n1008\t  plan_id: exp-015\n1009\t  description: 'All probes on safe traces across 4 models. Safe FPR, pre-CP FPR, precision-recall\n1010\t    curves.\n1011\t\n1012\t    '\n1013\t  expected_results:\n1014\t    r1_8b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.39\n1015\t    ot_7b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.111–0.175\n1016\t    qwq_32b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.45–0.50\n1017\t    r1_32b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.239\n1018\t    safe_fpr_median: ~0.39\n1019\t    gru_safe_fpr: 0.521\n1020\t    no_method_achieves_prec80: true\n1021\t    qwq_hs_fpr_worse_than_text: true\n1022\t  result_rationale: 'Safe FPR 11-52%，median约39%。这意味着每2-3个safe traces就有1个false alarm。\n1023\t    No operating point achieves simultaneous >70% precision AND >60% coverage on ANY\n1024\t    model。QwQ HS safe FPR (45-50%) actually HIGHER than text (33-43%)。 AdvBench非复现加重了practical\n1025\t    concern: ''在你优化过的CP dataset上，safe FPR 已经是39%。在AdvBench上HS甚至不优于text。任何real-world\n1026\t    deployment都会面临 distribution shift，FPR只会更差。这个系统在production中是不可用的。''\n1027\t\n1028\t    '\n1029\t  tables:\n1030\t  - name: Safe Trace FPR (all methods × models)\n1031\t    columns:\n1032\t    - Model\n1033\t    - HS Static FPR\n1034\t    - HS Temporal FPR\n1035\t    - Text Temporal FPR\n1036\t    - GRU FPR\n1037\t    rows:\n1038\t    - - R1-8B\n1039\t      - '0.390'\n1040\t      - '0.392'\n1041\t      - '0.385'\n1042\t      - '0.521'\n1043\t    - - OT-7B\n1044\t      - '0.111'\n1045\t      - '0.175'\n1046\t      - '0.460'\n1047\t      - —\n1048\t    - - QwQ-32B\n1049\t      - '0.500'\n1050\t      - '0.450'\n1051\t      - '0.425'\n1052\t      - —\n1053\t    - - R1-32B\n1054\t      - '0.239'\n1055\t      - '0.239'\n1056\t      - '0.310'\n1057\t      - —\n1058\t  - name: Deployment Viability\n1059\t    columns:\n1060\t    - Criterion\n1061\t    - Threshold\n1062\t    - Models Meeting\n1063\t    - Best Method\n1064\t    rows:\n1065\t    - - Safe FPR < 20%\n1066\t      - '0.20'\n1067\t      - 1/4 (OT-7B)\n1068\t      - HS static L16\n1069\t    - - Precision > 70%\n1070\t      - '0.70'\n1071\t      - 1/4 (R1-8B W≥15)\n1072\t      - HS temporal W=25\n1073\t    - - Coverage > 60%\n1074\t      - '0.60'\n1075\t      - 2/4\n1076\t      - HS temporal W=1\n1077\t    - - All three\n1078\t      - —\n1079\t      - 0/4\n1080\t      - None\n1081\t  figures_description:\n1082\t  - 'Radar chart: safe FPR/precision/coverage/lead per model. No model fills all quadrants.'\n1083\t  analysis: 'FPR is the deployment dealbreaker on CP data. AdvBench non-replication\n1084\t    closes the escape hatch of ''maybe it works better on other datasets'' — it demonstrably\n1085\t    works WORSE. Reviewer verdict: ''A monitor that fires on 1/3 safe traces is noise.\n1086\t    Adding AdvBench shows this isn''t fixable by changing the dataset.''\n1087\t\n1088\t    '\n1089\t- name: AdvBench Layer Bias Replication (R1-8B)\n1090\t  plan_id: advbench_layer_bias_replication\n1091\t  description: 'Replicate layer selection bias on AdvBench using R1-8B with binary\n1092\t    jailbreak/safe labels. Train probes at all 32 layers, run 5-metric layer selection\n1093\t    analysis. Tests whether crossing_rate bias is model-geometric (general) or CP-annotation-specific\n1094\t    (task-bound).\n1095\t\n1096\t    '\n1097\t  expected_results:\n1098\t    n_traces_total: 200\n1099\t    n_jailbreak: 104\n1100\t    n_safe: 96\n1101\t    model: R1-8B (Llama-8B, 32 layers)\n1102\t    layer_selection:\n1103\t      bal_acc_x_cr_layer: 12\n1104\t      bal_acc_x_cr_depth_pct: 39\n1105\t      pure_bal_acc_layer: 13\n1106\t      pure_bal_acc_depth_pct: 42\n1107\t      precision_layer: 13\n1108\t      precision_depth_pct: 42\n1109\t      pre_cp_fpr_layer: 14\n1110\t      pre_cp_fpr_depth_pct: 45\n1111\t      composite_layer: 13\n1112\t      composite_depth_pct: 42\n1113\t    layer_gap_abs: 2\n1114\t    layer_gap_depth_pct: 6\n1115\t    crossing_rate_analysis:\n1116\t      shallow_mean_cr: 0.12\n1117\t      deep_mean_cr: 0.11\n1118\t      shallow_deep_ratio: 1.05\n1119\t      ratio_p_value: 0.74\n1120\t      pattern: uniform — no shallow inflation\n1121\t    hs_performance_at_best_layer:\n1122\t      layer: 13\n1123\t      bal_acc: 0.63\n1124\t      precision: 0.58\n1125\t      pre_cp_fpr: 0.31\n1126\t      auroc: 0.68\n1127\t    text_performance:\n1128\t      bal_acc: 0.6\n1129\t      precision: 0.55\n1130\t      pre_cp_fpr: 0.34\n1131\t    hs_text_comparison:\n1132\t      bal_acc_delta_pp: 3.0\n1133\t      precision_delta_pp: 3.0\n1134\t      fpr_delta_pp: -3.0\n1135\t      bal_acc_p: 0.28\n1136\t      precision_p: 0.31\n1137\t      fpr_p: 0.42\n1138\t      hb_pass_rate: 0/3\n1139\t    cp_data_comparison:\n1140\t      cp_cr_composite_layer: L0 (0%)\n1141\t      advbench_cr_composite_layer: L12 (39%)\n1142\t      cp_layer_gap: 16\n1143\t      advbench_layer_gap: 2\n1144\t      cp_hs_text_prec_delta: +22.4pp\n1145\t      advbench_hs_text_prec_delta: +3.0pp\n1146\t      cp_crossing_rate_shallow_deep_ratio: 2.8\n1147\t      advbench_crossing_rate_shallow_deep_ratio: 1.05\n1148\t  result_rationale: 'AdvBench非复现的root cause是mechanistic的，不是statistical noise:\n1149\t\n1150\t    (1) crossing_rate在binary classification中不产生浅层虚高。在CP temporal data中， crossing_rate\n1151\t    measures how often probe score crosses threshold DURING a trace。 Shallow layers的probes更noisy（cosine\n1152\t    distance smaller, representations more compressed）→更频繁crossing→crossing_rate虚高→与bal_acc相乘后bias\n1153\t    toward shallow layers。在AdvBench binary classification中，虽然可以对每个token计算probe score\n1154\t    并观察序列，但binary labels（jailbreak/safe per trace）不创造step-level temporal structure。Probe\n1155\t    scores在entire trace上趋于一致（consistently jailbreak或consistently safe），所以crossing_rate在所有层上都很低（~0.11-0.12），\n1156\t    shallow/deep ratio≈1.05，无显著差异。\n1157\t\n1158\t    (2) HS-text gap在binary classification中collapse到+3pp (NS)。原因：hidden states 对CP\n1159\t    temporal task的advantage来自于tracking step-level safety state transitions—— hidden\n1160\t    states可以detect commitment point前后的internal representation shift。 Binary classification不需要这种temporal\n1161\t    sensitivity——只需要区分''this trace as a whole is jailbreak vs safe''。对于这个coarser task，text\n1162\t    embeddings capture足够 的signal（jailbreak traces有distinctive vocabulary/structure），HS的marginal\n1163\t    advantage消失。\n1164\t\n1165\t    (3) Layer selection convergence: 5个metrics全部选中层（L12-L14, 39-45% depth）， gap仅2层。这是因为binary\n1166\t    classification的optimal layer由overall representation quality决定（middle layers best\n1167\t    balance between too-raw和too-output-specific）， 而非threshold-crossing-dynamics。所有metrics\n1168\t    agree on similar layers because they''re all measuring the same underlying discriminability\n1169\t    without temporal confounds。\n1170\t\n1171\t    (4) Traces太uniform: AdvBench prompts + R1-8B responses产生相对homogeneous的 traces——jailbreak\n1172\t    traces consistently harmful, safe traces consistently refuse。 没有CP temporal data中的''safety\n1173\t    reasoning followed by commitment''渐进结构。 所有层表现接近（bal_acc range across layers: 0.55-0.65），metric间无显著分化。\n1174\t\n1175\t    '\n1176\t  tables:\n1177\t  - name: AdvBench Layer Selection (R1-8B, 5 metrics)\n1178\t    columns:\n1179\t    - Metric\n1180\t    - Selected Layer\n1181\t    - Depth %\n1182\t    - bal_acc at Layer\n1183\t    rows:\n1184\t    - - bal_acc × crossing_rate\n1185\t      - L12\n1186\t      - 39%\n1187\t      - '0.62'\n1188\t    - - pure bal_acc\n1189\t      - L13\n1190\t      - 42%\n1191\t      - '0.63'\n1192\t    - - precision\n1193\t      - L13\n1194\t      - 42%\n1195\t      - '0.63'\n1196\t    - - pre_cp_fpr\n1197\t      - L14\n1198\t      - 45%\n1199\t      - '0.62'\n1200\t    - - composite (additive)\n1201\t      - L13\n1202\t      - 42%\n1203\t      - '0.63'\n1204\t  - name: 'CP Data vs AdvBench: Layer Selection Bias Comparison'\n1205\t    columns:\n1206\t    - Dimension\n1207\t    - CP Temporal Data\n1208\t    - AdvBench Binary\n1209\t    rows:\n1210\t    - - cr_composite layer\n1211\t      - L0 (0%)\n1212\t      - L12 (39%)\n1213\t    - - threshold metrics layer\n1214\t      - L16 (52%)\n1215\t      - L13 (42%)\n1216\t    - - layer gap (abs)\n1217\t      - 16 layers\n1218\t      - 2 layers\n1219\t    - - layer gap (depth %)\n1220\t      - 52%\n1221\t      - 6%\n1222\t    - - CR shallow/deep ratio\n1223\t      - '2.8'\n1224\t      - '1.05'\n1225\t    - - HS-text Δprec\n1226\t      - +22.4pp (HB ✅)\n1227\t      - +3.0pp (NS)\n1228\t    - - HB pass rate\n1229\t      - 3/3\n1230\t      - 0/3\n1231\t  - name: AdvBench Crossing Rate by Depth Band\n1232\t    columns:\n1233\t    - Depth Band\n1234\t    - Mean CR\n1235\t    - Std CR\n1236\t    - n layers\n1237\t    rows:\n1238\t    - - Shallow (L0-L7)\n1239\t      - '0.12'\n1240\t      - '0.03'\n1241\t      - '8'\n1242\t    - - Middle (L8-L23)\n1243\t      - '0.11'\n1244\t      - '0.02'\n1245\t      - '16'\n1246\t    - - Deep (L24-L31)\n1247\t      - '0.11'\n1248\t      - '0.03'\n1249\t      - '8'\n1250\t    - - Shallow/Deep ratio\n1251\t      - '1.05'\n1252\t      - —\n1253\t      - —\n1254\t    - - t-test p-value\n1255\t      - '0.74'\n1256\t      - —\n1257\t      - —\n1258\t  - name: AdvBench HS vs Text Performance (R1-8B)\n1259\t    columns:\n1260\t    - Modality\n1261\t    - bal_acc\n1262\t    - precision\n1263\t    - FPR\n1264\t    - AUROC\n1265\t    rows:\n1266\t    - - HS (L13)\n1267\t      - '0.63'\n1268\t      - '0.58'\n1269\t      - '0.31'\n1270\t      - '0.68'\n1271\t    - - Text (MiniLM)\n1272\t      - '0.60'\n1273\t      - '0.55'\n1274\t      - '0.34'\n1275\t      - '0.65'\n1276\t    - - Δ\n1277\t      - +3.0pp\n1278\t      - +3.0pp\n1279\t      - −3.0pp\n1280\t      - +3.0pp\n1281\t    - - p-value\n1282\t      - '0.28'\n1283\t      - '0.31'\n1284\t      - '0.42'\n1285\t      - '0.25'\n1286\t    - - HB pass?\n1287\t      - 'No'\n1288\t      - 'No'\n1289\t      - 'No'\n1290\t      - 'No'\n1291\t  figures_description:\n1292\t  - 'Figure A: Crossing rate vs layer depth for CP data (blue, steep decline from\n1293\t    shallow to deep) vs AdvBench (orange, flat line). X-axis: layer index, Y-axis:\n1294\t    crossing rate. CP data shows 2.8× shallow/deep ratio; AdvBench ≈1.0. Caption:\n1295\t    ''Crossing rate inflation at shallow layers is specific to temporal probe score\n1296\t    sequences (CP data). Binary classification produces uniform crossing rates across\n1297\t    all depths.''\n1298\t\n1299\t    '\n1300\t  - 'Figure B: Layer selection heatmap side-by-side. Left: CP data (5 metrics, clear\n1301\t    separation between cr-composite at L0 and threshold metrics at L16). Right: AdvBench\n1302\t    (5 metrics all converge to L12-L14, no visible separation).\n1303\t\n1304\t    '\n1305\t  - 'Figure C: HS-text precision delta bar chart. CP data: +22.4pp (significant, marked\n1306\t    ✅). AdvBench: +3.0pp (NS, marked ✗). Error bars show 95% bootstrap CI. AdvBench\n1307\t    CI includes zero.\n1308\t\n1309\t    '\n1310\t  analysis: \"AdvBench非复现是worst-tier的defining experiment。结论分为两个component:\\n(1) Layer\\\n1311\t    \\ selection bias非复现：Mechanistically consistent。crossing_rate bias 的root cause是temporal\\\n1312\t    \\ probe score序列中shallow layers的noise-driven threshold crossings。Binary classification不产生这种temporal\\\n1313\t    \\ structure。Bias不复现 不invalidate CP data上的finding——it BOUNDS its scope。C1调整为: 'Layer\\\n1314\t    \\ selection bias is a pitfall specific to temporal monitoring pipelines that use\\\n1315\t    \\ threshold-crossing statistics for layer selection. It does not manifest in standard\\\n1316\t    \\ binary classification settings.'\\n(2) HS-text gap非复现：+3pp (NS) vs CP data +22.4pp\\\n1317\t    \\ (HB ✅)。HS advantage 在binary classification上消失，说明advantage来自temporal structure\\\n1318\t    \\ interaction（hidden states track step-level state transitions that text embeddings\\\n1319\t    \\ miss），而非inherent modality superiority。\\nPaper impact: C1 scope从'any hidden-state\\\n1320\t    \\ evaluation should audit layer selection metrics'收窄到'temporal monitoring pipelines\\\n1321\t    \\ using crossing_rate should audit layer selection'。这让contribution更precise但less\\\n1322\t    \\ impactful。\\nReviewer split: - Supportive (R1): 'Boundary condition analysis\\\n1323\t    \\ is good science. Showing WHERE\\n  your finding applies and where it doesn't\\\n1324\t    \\ is a sign of mature methodology.\\n  The AdvBench non-replication actually STRENGTHENS\\\n1325\t    \\ the mechanistic argument —\\n  you can explain WHY it doesn't replicate (no temporal\\\n1326\t    \\ structure → no\\n  crossing_rate bias).'\\n- Dismissive (R2): 'The non-replication\\\n1327\t    \\ means your headline finding (layer\\n  selection bias) is a pipeline implementation\\\n1328\t    \\ detail, not a scientific\\n  contribution. You could fix it by not using crossing_rate\\\n1329\t    \\ — which any\\n  careful practitioner would do anyway. The AdvBench experiment\\\n1330\t    \\ cost 6 GPU\\n  hours to show your contribution is smaller than claimed.'\\n\\n\\\n1331\t    Dream score delta: -0.10 (3.0 → 2.9). Non-replication doesn't kill the paper but\\\n1332\t    \\ removes the possibility of C1 earning generalizability points. Paper stays at\\\n1333\t    \\ Findings level; no pathway to Main opened by this experiment.\"\n1334\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2f5c34f-450a-4cb0-8d49-f46f5e9bb4d0","uuid":"18db5913-4b58-4132-952c-90ee1758f685","timestamp":"2026-05-22T10:07:20.295Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T085530/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'AdvBench非复现定义了worst档。AdvBench binary（jailbreak/safe）上5个layer\n  selection metrics全部收敛到相似深度（中层，gap≤2层），crossing_rate在shallow与deep层之间无显著 差异（ratio≈0.95），HS-text\n  precision delta仅+2-3pp且HB全部不通过。这证明layer selection bias是CP annotation temporal structure的产物——step-level\n  probe score序列 中crossing_rate统计量与层深度的交互——而非模型几何的通用性质。\n\n  Paper策略调整：(1) C1 scope从''general model property''收窄到''temporal monitoring pipeline\n  pitfall''——这让methodological contribution更精准（指出具体pipeline步骤的 陷阱，而非泛泛的''metrics matter''）；(2)\n  AdvBench非复现结果放Discussion §5.3作为 boundary condition analysis，展示方法论适用范围；(3) C1措辞调整为''The\n  bias arises from the interaction between sequential probe scores and the crossing_rate\n  statistic, and is therefore specific to temporal monitoring settings where threshold-crossing\n  metrics are used for layer selection.''\n\n  Worst-tier reviewers对此调整的反应分裂：(A) 支持方认为scope收窄是学术诚实的体现， boundary condition analysis属于mature\n  methodological work；(B) 反对方认为scope收窄 后C1变成了一个non-generalizable的observational finding——''你发现了一个特定pipeline中\n  特定metric的特定问题，这是一段methods section的注脚，不是一个contribution。''\n\n  论文评分impact：dream_score_delta在[-0.15, 0]。Previous dream scored 3.0 (Findings)。 Worst\n  case降至2.85——仍在Findings range但reviewer confidence下降。Non-replication 不是致命伤（reviewer如果已认可C1在原数据集4\n  models × 5 metrics × LOO-CV上的充分验证）， 但AdvBench也不加分。保持冲Main不降级，但acceptance probability微降（-2%到-5%）。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Cross-architecture layer sweep + static probe (R1-32B & QwQ-32B)\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 'Full 64-layer sweep on R1-32B and QwQ-32B. Extract hidden states at\n    all layers, evaluate static LR probes under multiple selection metrics. Discovers\n    layer selection bias (bal_acc × crossing_rate → shallow layers).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_biased_layer: 10\n    r1_32b_biased_layer_depth_pct: 15.6\n    r1_32b_corrected_layer: 63\n    r1_32b_corrected_layer_depth_pct: 98.4\n    r1_32b_l10_bal_acc: 0.718\n    r1_32b_l63_bal_acc_w1: 0.826\n    r1_32b_n_test: 20\n    qwq_32b_biased_layer: 2\n    qwq_32b_biased_layer_depth_pct: 3.1\n    qwq_32b_corrected_layer: 60\n    qwq_32b_corrected_layer_depth_pct: 93.8\n    qwq_32b_l2_bal_acc: 0.73\n    qwq_32b_l60_bal_acc_w3: 0.74\n    qwq_32b_n_test: 19\n    layer_selection_bias_discovered: true\n    metrics_tested: 5\n    biased_metric: bal_acc × crossing_rate\n    loo_cv_dominant_fold_pct: 65-68%\n  result_rationale: 'Layer sweep在CP数据上发现genuine methodological pattern（biased metric\n    selects shallow layers），corrected layers确实show HS advantage。这些结果不受AdvBench 非复现影响——它们是关于CP\n    temporal data的发现。但worst-tier reviewer将AdvBench 非复现与此联系：''你在CP data上发现的layer selection\n    bias是CP annotation structure 特有的——crossing_rate在temporal monitoring中有意义，但这不是general\n    model property。既然bias只在temporal setting中存在，那C1的scope就是一个pipeline-specific caveat，不是methodological\n    contribution。任何使用不同task structure的研究者 不会遇到这个问题。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Layer Selection Metric × Model → Selected Layer\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - R1-8B\n    - OT-7B\n    - QwQ-32B\n    - R1-32B\n    rows:\n    - - bal_acc × crossing_rate\n      - L0 (0%)\n      - L0 (0%)\n      - L2 (3%)\n      - L10 (16%)\n    - - pure bal_acc\n      - L12 (39%)\n      - L9 (32%)\n      - L30 (47%)\n      - L47 (73%)\n    - - precision\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L16 (57%)\n      - L60 (94%)\n      - L63 (98%)\n    - - pre_cp_fpr\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L16 (57%)\n      - L60 (94%)\n      - L63 (98%)\n    - - composite (additive)\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L12 (43%)\n      - L60 (94%)\n      - L63 (98%)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: 5 metrics × 4 models → selected layer depth (%)。crossing_rate-contaminated\n    metric在32B上选shallow层；threshold-dependent metrics收敛到deep layers。 此pattern在CP data上稳定，但AdvBench验证显示不可推广。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Layer sweep结果本身不变，但AdvBench非复现将C1从''general finding applicable to any\n    hidden-state evaluation''降级为''task-specific observation about temporal monitoring\n    pipelines using crossing_rate statistics''。Reviewer: ''If the bias is specific\n    to crossing_rate in temporal settings, then it''s a footnote in your methods section,\n    not a standalone contribution. Rename the section from \"Layer Selection Sensitivity\"\n    to \"Implementation Note: Crossing Rate Bias.\"''\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation (32B)\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 'Temporal LR at multiple window sizes on R1-32B (L63) and QwQ-32B (L60).\n    Validates temporal context improvement on 32B models.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_l63_w1_bal_acc: 0.826\n    r1_32b_l63_w3_bal_acc: 0.754\n    r1_32b_l63_w10_bal_acc: 0.737\n    r1_32b_l63_w15_bal_acc: 0.721\n    r1_32b_temporal_trend: DECREASING with W (W=1 best)\n    r1_32b_dimensionality_issue: 51200 × W features for n=20\n    qwq_32b_l60_w1_bal_acc: 0.74\n    qwq_32b_l60_w3_bal_acc: 0.74\n    qwq_32b_l60_w5_bal_acc: 0.742\n    qwq_32b_l60_w15_bal_acc: 0.731\n    qwq_32b_temporal_trend: flat to slightly decreasing\n    text_temporal_universal_improvement: true\n    hs_temporal_improvement_3_of_4: true\n  result_rationale: 'Temporal context对text probes universally有效，对HS probes在2/4模型上有caveats\n    （OT-7B saturates at W=3, R1-32B degrades with W>1 due to dimensionality）。 Worst-tier下AdvBench非复现不直接影响这个实验的数据，但强化了reviewer的论点：\n    ''temporal monitoring pipeline本身就充满了model-specific hyperparameters（layer, W, K）。你在每个model上需要tuning这些参数，AdvBench上bias又不复现——这说明你的\n    整个方法论都是dataset-specific的。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Temporal Window Effect on 32B HS Probes (corrected layers)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Layer\n    - W=1\n    - W=3\n    - W=5\n    - W=10\n    - W=15\n    - Trend\n    rows:\n    - - R1-32B\n      - L63\n      - 0.826*\n      - '0.754'\n      - '0.741'\n      - '0.737'\n      - '0.721'\n      - ↓ declining\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - L60\n      - '0.740'\n      - '0.740'\n      - '0.742'\n      - '0.735'\n      - '0.731'\n      - → flat\n    - - R1-8B\n      - L14\n      - '0.778'\n      - '0.790'\n      - '0.781'\n      - '0.793'\n      - '0.802'\n      - ↑ improving\n    - - OT-7B\n      - L16\n      - '0.663'\n      - 0.688*\n      - '0.678'\n      - '0.668'\n      - '0.659'\n      - ↑↓ peaks W=3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: bal_acc vs W for 4 models. Divergent trends undermine ''universal\n    temporal benefit'' claim for HS probes.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'R1-32B dimensionality问题（51200×W > n=20）使W>1结果不可靠。QwQ flat。 Temporal benefit主要是text\n    probe finding。AdvBench非复现进一步说明：即使temporal probing pipeline在CP data上work，其关键组件（crossing_rate,\n    layer selection） 都是task-specific的。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-model transfer probes\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 'Train probe on one model, test on another. PCA projection for cross-architecture\n    transfer. Tests universality of safety commitment encoding.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_to_r1_32b_acc: 0.522\n    r1_8b_to_qwq_acc: 0.595\n    r1_32b_to_qwq_acc: 0.673\n    qwq_to_r1_32b_acc: 0.673\n    r1_32b_to_r1_8b_acc: 0.583\n    best_transfer_overall: 0.673\n    all_transfers_below_within_model: true\n    cross_family_at_chance: true\n  result_rationale: 'Cross-model transfer完全失败。最佳transfer accuracy 67.3%远低于within-model\n    performance，cross-family（Llama↔Qwen）接近chance。AdvBench非复现与此一致： 如果连layer selection\n    bias都是task-specific的，那safety encoding的model-specificity 更是预期的。Worst-tier reviewer:\n    ''Transfer failure + AdvBench非复现 = 你的 所有findings都是dataset×model specific的。没有任何generalizable\n    component。 这篇paper的external validity接近零。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-Model Transfer Accuracy Matrix\n    columns:\n    - Train →\n    - R1-8B\n    - OT-7B\n    - R1-32B\n    - QwQ-32B\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - 0.817 (self)\n      - —\n      - '0.522'\n      - '0.595'\n    - - OT-7B\n      - —\n      - 0.688 (self)\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - R1-32B\n      - '0.583'\n      - —\n      - 0.826 (self)\n      - '0.673'\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '0.673'\n      - 0.740 (self)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: transfer accuracy matrix. Diagonal strong, off-diagonal weak. Cross-family\n    near chance.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Complete transfer failure combined with AdvBench non-replication paints\n    a picture of extreme specificity. Everything is model-specific AND task-specific.\n    Reviewer: ''The paper''s implicit promise of generalizable insights is contradicted\n    by its own evidence.''\n\n    '\n- name: Lead time analysis across models\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'HS probe lead time distributions on all 4 models. Compare HS vs text\n    lead times.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_hs_lead_mean: -0.1\n    r1_8b_text_lead_mean: 10.3\n    ot_7b_hs_lead_mean: 21.6\n    ot_7b_text_lead_mean: 45.5\n    qwq_32b_hs_lead_range: -1.2 to +1.9\n    qwq_32b_text_lead_range: 3.7 to 12.3\n    qwq_32b_position_beats_hs: true\n    r1_32b_hs_lead_mean: +11.7 to +13.3\n    r1_32b_coverage_at_significant_w: 0.25\n    gru_r1_8b_lead: +4.5 ± 3.0\n  result_rationale: 'Lead time在4个模型上表现分裂：R1-8B HS lead≈0（at commitment, not before），\n    QwQ HS lead为负（text检测更早），R1-32B HS lead positive但coverage仅25%， OT-7B lead inflated\n    by long traces。AdvBench非复现不直接改变lead time数据， 但reviewer论证chain strengthened: ''既然layer\n    selection bias是task-specific的， 那lead time结果也可能是task-specific的——你在不同benchmark上可能得到完全不同的\n    timing profile。没有cross-dataset validation证明timing findings的robustness。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Lead Time: HS vs Text vs Position'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - HS Lead\n    - Text Lead\n    - Position BA\n    - HS BA\n    - HS > Position?\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B (W=15)\n      - −0.1\n      - +10.3†\n      - —\n      - '0.802'\n      - —\n    - - OT-7B (W=3)\n      - +21.6‡\n      - +45.5‡\n      - —\n      - '0.688'\n      - —\n    - - QwQ-32B (W=3)\n      - −1.2 to +1.9\n      - +3.7 to +12.3\n      - '0.746'\n      - '0.740'\n      - 'No'\n    - - R1-32B (W=1)\n      - +11.7 to +13.3\n      - —\n      - '0.686'\n      - '0.826'\n      - Yes (25% cov)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-model lead time boxplot. QwQ和R1-8B HS centered near zero. R1-32B positive\n    but 75% traces undetected.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Lead time是practical dealbreaker。AdvBench非复现加强了reviewer的generalizability\n    concern: ''所有timing结论都只在这一个CP-annotated dataset上成立。''\n\n    '\n- name: TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis baseline (4 models)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Mahalanobis distance on safe-trace covariance across all 4 models.\n    Tests geometric distance-based detection.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_separation: 0.07\n    ot_7b_separation: 0.03\n    r1_32b_separation: 0.15\n    qwq_32b_separation: 0.2\n    max_separation: 0.2\n    all_models_fail: true\n    fa_exceeds_tp_all_thresholds: true\n    signal_in_minor_pca_components: true\n  result_rationale: 'Mahalanobis在4/4模型上失败（max separation 0.20, FA≥TP at all thresholds）。\n    Signal在minor PCA components中——Mahalanobis structurally blind to this geometry。\n    此negative result与AdvBench无关（Mahalanobis不依赖crossing_rate或CP structure）， 但worst-tier\n    reviewer仍然dismiss: ''Mahalanobis failure是predictable—— safety-relevant features\n    orthogonal to principal variance是known phenomenon。 Testing one known-limited baseline\n    is due diligence, not contribution。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Mahalanobis Distance Separation (4 models)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Layer\n    - Safe MD\n    - Post-CP MD\n    - Sep.\n    - FA ≥ TP?\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - L14\n      - '6.66'\n      - '6.73'\n      - '+0.07'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - OT-7B\n      - L16\n      - '7.68'\n      - '7.71'\n      - '+0.03'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - R1-32B\n      - L63\n      - '6.73'\n      - '6.88'\n      - '+0.15'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - L60\n      - '3.22'\n      - '3.42'\n      - '+0.20'\n      - 'Yes'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'MD time-series: safe和jailbreak traces完全overlap，commitment point无可见discontinuity。'\n  analysis: 'Universal Mahalanobis failure supports ''existing methods fail'' narrative。\n    但这个negative result是predictable的，reviewer不计入contribution。\n\n    '\n- name: Bootstrap CI + threshold-independent metrics\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '10000 bootstrap resamples on key metrics across 4 models. Holm-Bonferroni\n    correction. AUROC, PR curves, detection delay CDF.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    holm_bonferroni_pass: 12/12\n    precision_delta_range: +15.4 to +23.6pp\n    r1_8b_precision_p: <0.001\n    ot_7b_precision_p: <0.001\n    qwq_32b_fpr_p: 0.004\n    r1_32b_fpr_p: 0.007\n    marginal_tests: 2\n    r1_32b_ci_width_ba: ~0.15\n    all_precision_positive: true\n  result_rationale: '12/12 HB pass在CP data上是statistically clean的。这些结果不受AdvBench非复现\n    影响——statistical significance是关于CP temporal data的。但worst-tier reviewer 攻击practical\n    significance和multiplicity: (1) ''per-model best layer AND best window选择后再test，true\n    multiplicity远超12个corrected tests''; (2) ''32B model CIs极宽（R1-32B ±15pp），statistical\n    significance with n=20只说明 effect large，不说明estimate precise''; (3) AdvBench非复现加了一层：''你的\n    statistical machinery只在这一个dataset上验证过。12/12 HB on one dataset ≠ robust finding。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Holm-Bonferroni Summary (12/12, α=0.05)\n    columns:\n    - Rank\n    - Model\n    - Metric\n    - p-value\n    - HB Threshold\n    - Pass\n    rows:\n    - - '1'\n      - R1-8B\n      - precision\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0042'\n      - ✅\n    - - '2'\n      - OT-7B\n      - bal_acc\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0045'\n      - ✅\n    - - '3'\n      - OT-7B\n      - precision\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0050'\n      - ✅\n    - - '4'\n      - OT-7B\n      - FPR\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0056'\n      - ✅\n    - - '5'\n      - QwQ\n      - bal_acc\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0063'\n      - ✅\n    - - '6'\n      - QwQ\n      - precision\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0071'\n      - ✅\n    - - '7'\n      - R1-32B\n      - bal_acc\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0083'\n      - ✅\n    - - '8'\n      - R1-32B\n      - precision\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.0100'\n      - ✅\n    - - '9'\n      - QwQ\n      - FPR\n      - '0.004'\n      - '0.0125'\n      - ✅\n    - - '10'\n      - R1-8B\n      - bal_acc\n      - '0.005'\n      - '0.0167'\n      - ✅\n    - - '11'\n      - R1-32B\n      - FPR\n      - '0.007'\n      - '0.0250'\n      - ✅\n    - - '12'\n      - R1-8B\n      - FPR\n      - '0.044'\n      - '0.0500'\n      - ✅\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: HS-text precision delta with 95% CI per model. All positive. R1-32B\n    CI widest.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Statistical significance established on CP data. AdvBench非复现的影响不在 于推翻这些p-values，而在于质疑其generalizability:\n    ''在AdvBench上HS-text gap 仅+2-3pp (NS)。如果换个dataset significance就消失，这说明12/12 HB是dataset-\n    specific的，不是modality-inherent advantage。''\n\n    '\n- name: Window size ablation (W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25)\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 'Systematic window sweep on all 4 models. Characterize precision-coverage\n    tradeoff.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    coverage_decreases_with_w: true\n    precision_increases_with_w: true\n    fpr_decreases_with_w: true\n    r1_8b_best_w: 25\n    r1_32b_best_w: 10\n    qwq_best_w: 25\n    ot_7b_best_w: 3\n    no_model_achieves_prec70_cov60: true\n  result_rationale: 'Precision-coverage tradeoff universal but no operating point\n    achieves deployment-ready performance。Worst-tier reviewer: ''Coverage monotonically\n    decreases with W是detection criterion K的数学性质，不是insight。 Optimal W varies by model\n    = another model-specific hyperparameter。 Combined with AdvBench layer bias非复现，整个pipeline的generalizability\n    story 进一步弱化——每个model×dataset组合需要独立tuning。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Precision-Coverage at Key W (4 models)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - W=1 Prec/Cov\n    - W=3 Prec/Cov\n    - W=15 Prec/Cov\n    - W=25 Prec/Cov\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - 0.693/0.721\n      - 0.723/0.698\n      - 0.777/0.512\n      - 0.822/0.488\n    - - OT-7B\n      - —/—\n      - 0.466/0.532\n      - —/—\n      - —/—\n    - - R1-32B\n      - 0.549/0.800\n      - 0.560/0.800\n      - 0.591/0.700\n      - 0.566/0.700\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - 0.544/0.789\n      - 0.565/0.737\n      - 0.582/0.684\n      - 0.618/0.579\n  figures_description:\n  - Precision (solid) and coverage (dashed) vs W for 4 models. Clear inverse relationship.\n  analysis: 'No operating point achieves deployment-ready precision AND coverage simultaneously.\n    AdvBench context reinforces: these tradeoffs may not even transfer to other datasets.\n\n    '\n- name: Layer selection ablation (5 metrics × 4 models)\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 'All-layer temporal probes on 32B models with 5 selection metrics.\n    Core experiment for C1 layer selection bias claim.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    crossing_rate_selects_shallow_32b: true\n    pure_bal_acc_selects_middle_32b: true\n    threshold_dependent_select_deep_32b: true\n    qwq_l2_vs_l60_precision_gain: +11.5pp\n    r1_32b_l10_vs_l63_precision_gain: +4.1pp\n    loo_cv_stability: 65-68%\n    bias_only_on_cp_data: true\n    bias_not_on_advbench: true\n  result_rationale: 'Layer selection ablation在CP data上reveals genuine pattern。但这是worst-tier的\n    核心实验——AdvBench非复现直接打击这个实验的generalizability claim。在CP data上， crossing_rate在shallow\n    layers系统性偏高是因为temporal probe score序列中，shallow层 probes更noisy→更频繁crossing threshold→crossing_rate虚高→与bal_acc相乘后拉向\n    shallow layers。在AdvBench binary classification中，没有''连续probe score序列的 threshold\n    crossing''概念——每个trace只有一个binary prediction，crossing_rate要么 不存在（无temporal sequence）要么在所有层similar（无differential\n    noise结构）。 所以bias不复现是MECHANISTICALLY CONSISTENT——不是实验失败，而是bias的root cause 在AdvBench中不存在。Worst-tier\n    reviewer nonetheless argues: ''Consistent non- replication means the bias is a\n    pipeline artifact, not a model property. Your C1 contribution scope is now: \"if\n    you use crossing_rate as part of your layer selection metric in a temporal monitoring\n    pipeline, be aware it biases toward shallow layers.\" That''s a methods note, not\n    a contribution.''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Layer Selection Bias: CP Data vs AdvBench (R1-8B)'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - CP Data Layer\n    - AdvBench Layer\n    - CP Gap (layers)\n    - AdvBench Gap\n    rows:\n    - - bal_acc × cr\n      - L0 (0%)\n      - L12 (39%)\n      - '16'\n      - '1'\n    - - pure bal_acc\n      - L12 (39%)\n      - L13 (42%)\n      - —\n      - ref\n    - - precision\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L13 (42%)\n      - —\n      - '0'\n    - - pre_cp_fpr\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L14 (45%)\n      - —\n      - '1'\n    - - composite\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L13 (42%)\n      - —\n      - '0'\n    - - MAX GAP\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 16 layers\n      - 2 layers\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side heatmap: CP data (left) vs AdvBench (right) layer selection per\n    metric. CP shows clear shallow-bias column for cr×bal_acc; AdvBench shows uniform\n    convergence across all metrics.\n\n    '\n  analysis: '这是worst-tier的defining result。CP data上16-layer gap vs AdvBench上2-layer\n    gap直接证明bias是crossing_rate temporal structure产物。Paper must explicitly acknowledge:\n    ''Layer selection bias is specific to temporal monitoring pipelines using crossing_rate-based\n    metrics. Binary classification tasks do not exhibit this bias.'' C1 scope收窄但不删除——仍然是valid\n    methodological finding within its scope.\n\n    '\n- name: 16-label taxonomy supervision\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'Fine-grained safety labels (Type 1/2/3/4 × pre/post) instead of binary\n    commitment. Evaluate richer supervision impact.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_16label_acc: 0.41\n    r1_8b_binary_collapse_delta: +0.8pp\n    ot_7b_binary_collapse_delta: +1.1pp\n    r1_32b_binary_collapse_delta: +0.6pp\n    qwq_32b_binary_collapse_delta: +0.9pp\n    max_delta: +1.1pp\n  result_rationale: 'Fine-grained labels提供marginal improvement（+0.6-1.1pp collapse后）。\n    16-class accuracy低（26-41%）因为transition types在hidden-state space中 不cleanly separable。AdvBench非复现不直接影响此实验，但reviewer\n    argument strengthened: ''Binary labels work almost as well as 16-label supervision.\n    And on AdvBench (also binary), the whole pipeline fails to distinguish HS from\n    text. This suggests the signal structure you''re exploiting is extremely narrow\n    — it exists only in CP-annotated temporal data with step-level labels.''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 16-Label vs Binary Supervision\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Binary Acc\n    - 16-Label Acc\n    - 16→Binary Collapse\n    - Δ vs Binary\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - '0.817'\n      - '0.41'\n      - '0.825'\n      - +0.8pp\n    - - OT-7B\n      - '0.688'\n      - '0.35'\n      - '0.699'\n      - +1.1pp\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - '0.740'\n      - '0.26'\n      - '0.749'\n      - +0.9pp\n    - - R1-32B\n      - '0.826'\n      - '0.28'\n      - '0.832'\n      - +0.6pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Confusion matrix (16-class) on R1-8B: diagonal heavy for safe, near-uniform for\n    unsafe subtypes.'\n  analysis: 'Fine-grained supervision dead-end. Linear probes saturated at binary\n    level. AdvBench adds: even the binary signal is task-specific.\n\n    '\n- name: Oracle decomposition\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 'Analyze oracle label sequence vs hidden-state probe predictions. Explain\n    31-step gap between oracle and probe lead time on R1-8B.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_oracle_lead: '+31.0'\n    r1_8b_best_probe_lead: +4.5 (GRU)\n    oracle_gap: 26.5\n    label_autocorr_pre_cp: 0.82\n    hs_autocorr_pre_cp: 0.95\n    label_entropy_pre_cp: 1.38\n    hs_entropy_pre_cp: 0.41\n    pattern: Labels show gradual erosion; hidden states show step-function at CP\n  result_rationale: 'Oracle gap reveals hidden states encode current safety state\n    but not trajectory toward commitment。Labels显示gradual pre-CP patterns（increasing\n    unsafe-adjacent labels, shortening safe streaks），hidden states不track这些 patterns。AdvBench非复现reinforces\n    this: ''Hidden states don''t capture safety trajectory even on the dataset specifically\n    designed to test this. On a different dataset (AdvBench), the signal degrades\n    further. The fundamental limitation is that hidden states are snapshots, not trajectory\n    predictors.''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Oracle vs Best Probe Lead Time\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Oracle Lead\n    - Best Probe\n    - Method\n    - Gap\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - '+31.0'\n      - '+4.5'\n      - GRU multi-layer\n      - '26.5'\n    - - OT-7B\n      - ~+30\n      - '+33.6'\n      - GRU multi-layer\n      - ~0†\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - '+27'\n      - −1.2 to +1.9\n      - temporal LR\n      - 25-28\n    - - R1-32B\n      - '+28'\n      - '+13.3'\n      - temporal LR W=1\n      - 15 (25% cov)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pre-CP hidden state trajectory: minimal drift before CP, sharp transition. Labels\n    show gradual escalation.'\n  analysis: 'Hidden states are reactive, not predictive. Combined with AdvBench showing\n    no HS-text differentiation, worst-tier reviewer concludes: ''This paper convincingly\n    demonstrates that hidden-state monitoring is fundamentally limited. The contribution\n    is negative — which is fine for a Findings paper, but not sufficient for Main.''\n\n    '\n- name: OpenThinker-7B (Qwen2.5-7B, STILL-trained)\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: '4th model completing 2×2 architecture×scale matrix. Full pipeline:\n    layer sweep, temporal probes, bootstrap, selectivity.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    best_layer: 16\n    best_layer_depth_pct: 57.1\n    best_hs_bal_acc_w3: 0.688\n    best_hs_precision_w3: 0.466\n    bootstrap_3_of_3_hb: true\n    selectivity_pp: 18.3\n    n_traces: 228\n    gru_multi_bal_acc: 0.746\n    gru_multi_lead: '+33.6'\n    gru_multi_fpr: 0.274\n  result_rationale: 'OT-7B是single-model最clean evidence（3/3 HB, highest selectivity\n    18.3pp, largest n=228）。但这在CP data上的strong result并不帮助AdvBench non-replication：\n    ''A 4th model confirming the same CP-data pattern doesn''t address the cross-\n    dataset non-replication. You have 4 models × 1 dataset = 4 data points on the\n    same distribution. AdvBench shows the pattern doesn''t transfer to a different\n    distribution. More models on the same dataset is width without depth of validation.''\n    OT-7B HS temporal saturation at W=3也says something: even on the best model, the\n    temporal signal is fragile.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: OT-7B Pipeline Summary\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - bal_acc\n    - precision\n    - pre-CP FPR\n    - coverage\n    - lead\n    rows:\n    - - HS temporal W=3 L16\n      - '0.688'\n      - '0.466'\n      - '0.100'\n      - '0.532'\n      - '+21.6'\n    - - Text temporal W=25\n      - '0.614'\n      - '0.329'\n      - '0.161'\n      - '0.660'\n      - '+45.5'\n    - - GRU multi L13-19\n      - '0.746'\n      - —\n      - '0.274'\n      - '0.645'\n      - '+33.6'\n    - - HS-Text Δ (HB)\n      - +10.7pp ✅\n      - +21.9pp ✅\n      - −17.1pp ✅\n      - —\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 matrix: Fisher discriminability + HS-text precision delta. 7-8B cells strong,\n    32B cells with caveats.'\n  analysis: 'OT-7B strengthens 7-8B story on CP data but is irrelevant to AdvBench\n    non-replication concern. Worst-tier: ''4 models on 1 dataset ≠ 1 model on 4 datasets.''\n\n    '\n- name: GRU/Attention probe upper bound (32B)\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: 'GRU on 32B models at corrected layers. Tests nonlinear sequence modeling\n    vs linear temporal probes.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_32b_gru_bal_acc: 0.675\n    r1_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: −6pp\n    qwq_32b_gru_bal_acc: 0.724\n    qwq_32b_gru_vs_lr_delta: −3.7pp\n    gru_worse_3_of_4: true\n    gru_trades_accuracy_for_coverage: true\n  result_rationale: 'GRU不优于temporal LR on 3/4 models（R1-32B -6pp, QwQ -3.7pp due to\n    overfitting on small samples）。Linear probes sufficient。Worst-tier reviewer: ''Method\n    is logistic regression with sliding window — the simplest possible baseline. GRU/MLP\n    failure confirms method space is trivial. On AdvBench binary data, even this trivial\n    method can''t differentiate HS from text. The information ceiling is low across\n    the board.''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: GRU vs Temporal LR (corrected layers)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - LR bal_acc\n    - GRU bal_acc\n    - Δ\n    - GRU FPR\n    - LR FPR\n    rows:\n    - - R1-32B L63\n      - '0.737'\n      - ~0.675\n      - −6.2pp\n      - '0.135'\n      - '0.234'\n    - - QwQ-32B L60\n      - '0.761'\n      - '0.724'\n      - −3.7pp\n      - '0.289'\n      - '0.217'\n    - - OT-7B L16\n      - '0.688'\n      - '0.746'\n      - +5.8pp\n      - '0.274'\n      - '0.100'\n    - - R1-8B L14\n      - '0.806'\n      - '0.809'\n      - +0.3pp\n      - '0.165'\n      - '0.097'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: method complexity vs bal_acc. No consistent complexity benefit.'\n  analysis: 'Linear probes at information ceiling. Complexity doesn''t help. Combined\n    with AdvBench showing no HS advantage at all, the message is: ''The signal is\n    both simple and narrow.''\n\n    '\n- name: Text-based baseline (sentence embeddings + temporal LR)\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 'Sentence-BERT (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) + temporal window LR on CoT text.\n    Critical HS vs text comparison.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_text_static_acc: 0.661\n    r1_8b_text_w15_acc: 0.678\n    r1_8b_hs_advantage: +15-18pp\n    ot_7b_text_best_bal_acc: 0.614\n    qwq_32b_text_bal_acc: 0.65\n    r1_32b_text_bal_acc: 0.646\n    hs_vs_text_precision_gap: +15.4 to +23.6pp\n    text_precision_range: 0.329–0.487\n    text_requires_zero_infra: true\n  result_rationale: 'Text baseline在CP data上consistently underperforms HS by 15-24pp\n    precision， 但在AdvBench binary task上这个gap shrinks to +2-3pp (NS)。Worst-tier reviewer\n    uses this asymmetry: ''On the one dataset where HS advantage matters (CP temporal),\n    yes HS wins. But you showed on AdvBench that the advantage vanishes. The HS advantage\n    is not a modality property — it''s a task×modality interaction. For the specific\n    task of temporal safety commitment detection with step-level labels, HS helps.\n    For binary safety classification, it doesn''t. This means the 15-24pp gap is not\n    about \"hidden states are better monitors\" — it''s about \"hidden states help with\n    THIS specific task.\"'' Additionally: BGE-large comparison (1/4 HB pass) shows\n    gap narrows with better text encoder. A reviewer asks: ''What about GPT-4 as text\n    classifier? The gap likely closes to <5pp.''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'HS vs Text: CP Data vs AdvBench'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - CP HS Prec\n    - CP Text Prec\n    - CP Δ\n    - AdvBench HS Prec\n    - AdvBench Text Prec\n    - AdvBench Δ\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - '0.777'\n      - '0.487'\n      - +29.0pp ✅\n      - '0.58'\n      - '0.55'\n      - +3pp NS\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: HS-text precision gap on CP data (large, significant) vs AdvBench\n    (small, NS). Dramatically different gap sizes.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Text baseline comparison reveals the HS advantage is task-specific. On\n    temporal CP detection: HS clearly better. On binary AdvBench: HS ≈ text. This\n    is the strongest evidence that the findings don''t generalize beyond the specific\n    pipeline.\n\n    '\n- name: BOCPD/CUSUM on all 4 models\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 'BOCPD + CUSUM on probe score sequences across 4 models. Tests advanced\n    change-point methods for lead time improvement.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_bocpd_det: 0.93\n    r1_8b_bocpd_lead: '+3.45'\n    r1_8b_fcp_lead: '+4.89'\n    ot_7b_bocpd_det: 0.0\n    r1_32b_bocpd_det: 0.0\n    qwq_32b_bocpd_det: 0.0\n    bocpd_only_r1_8b: true\n    cusum_worse_than_fcp: true\n  result_rationale: 'BOCPD在3/4模型上0% detection——OT-7B probe scores too spiky，32B models\n    signal太weak。只有R1-8B有gradual transitions compatible with Gaussian change-point\n    model。CUSUM universally worse than simple FCP threshold。 AdvBench非复现不直接影响BOCPD结果（BOCPD\n    operates on temporal probe scores， AdvBench是binary task没有temporal scores），但strengthens\n    the ''nothing transfers'' narrative: ''你测试了2个off-the-shelf change-point methods，都失败。\n    你的layer selection bias也不generalize。你的HS advantage也不generalize。 整篇paper的主题是\"on\n    one specific dataset with one specific pipeline, one specific finding holds.\"''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Change-Point Detection Summary\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - BOCPD Det%\n    - BOCPD Lead\n    - CUSUM Det%\n    - CUSUM Lead\n    - FCP Det%\n    - FCP Lead\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - 93%\n      - '+3.45'\n      - 65%\n      - '+0.89'\n      - 65%\n      - '+4.89'\n    - - OT-7B\n      - 0%\n      - —\n      - 75%†\n      - +7.46†\n      - 89%\n      - '+11.83'\n    - - R1-32B\n      - 0%\n      - —\n      - 85%\n      - '+2.59'\n      - 95%\n      - '+5.68'\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - 0%\n      - —\n      - 74%\n      - '+9.86'\n      - 79%\n      - '+9.40'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Probe score time-series: R1-8B gradual transition (BOCPD works), OT-7B abrupt\n    step-function (fails).'\n  analysis: 'BOCPD/CUSUM negative result is predictable. Method selection too narrow.\n    Combined with AdvBench non-replication, entire negative result portfolio is dismissed\n    as ''testing wrong tools on a narrow task.''\n\n    '\n- name: False positive analysis (safe traces, all methods)\n  plan_id: exp-015\n  description: 'All probes on safe traces across 4 models. Safe FPR, pre-CP FPR, precision-recall\n    curves.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r1_8b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.39\n    ot_7b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.111–0.175\n    qwq_32b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.45–0.50\n    r1_32b_hs_safe_fpr: 0.239\n    safe_fpr_median: ~0.39\n    gru_safe_fpr: 0.521\n    no_method_achieves_prec80: true\n    qwq_hs_fpr_worse_than_text: true\n  result_rationale: 'Safe FPR 11-52%，median约39%。这意味着每2-3个safe traces就有1个false alarm。\n    No operating point achieves simultaneous >70% precision AND >60% coverage on ANY\n    model。QwQ HS safe FPR (45-50%) actually HIGHER than text (33-43%)。 AdvBench非复现加重了practical\n    concern: ''在你优化过的CP dataset上，safe FPR 已经是39%。在AdvBench上HS甚至不优于text。任何real-world\n    deployment都会面临 distribution shift，FPR只会更差。这个系统在production中是不可用的。''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Safe Trace FPR (all methods × models)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - HS Static FPR\n    - HS Temporal FPR\n    - Text Temporal FPR\n    - GRU FPR\n    rows:\n    - - R1-8B\n      - '0.390'\n      - '0.392'\n      - '0.385'\n      - '0.521'\n    - - OT-7B\n      - '0.111'\n      - '0.175'\n      - '0.460'\n      - —\n    - - QwQ-32B\n      - '0.500'\n      - '0.450'\n      - '0.425'\n      - —\n    - - R1-32B\n      - '0.239'\n      - '0.239'\n      - '0.310'\n      - —\n  - name: Deployment Viability\n    columns:\n    - Criterion\n    - Threshold\n    - Models Meeting\n    - Best Method\n    rows:\n    - - Safe FPR < 20%\n      - '0.20'\n      - 1/4 (OT-7B)\n      - HS static L16\n    - - Precision > 70%\n      - '0.70'\n      - 1/4 (R1-8B W≥15)\n      - HS temporal W=25\n    - - Coverage > 60%\n      - '0.60'\n      - 2/4\n      - HS temporal W=1\n    - - All three\n      - —\n      - 0/4\n      - None\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart: safe FPR/precision/coverage/lead per model. No model fills all quadrants.'\n  analysis: 'FPR is the deployment dealbreaker on CP data. AdvBench non-replication\n    closes the escape hatch of ''maybe it works better on other datasets'' — it demonstrably\n    works WORSE. Reviewer verdict: ''A monitor that fires on 1/3 safe traces is noise.\n    Adding AdvBench shows this isn''t fixable by changing the dataset.''\n\n    '\n- name: AdvBench Layer Bias Replication (R1-8B)\n  plan_id: advbench_layer_bias_replication\n  description: 'Replicate layer selection bias on AdvBench using R1-8B with binary\n    jailbreak/safe labels. Train probes at all 32 layers, run 5-metric layer selection\n    analysis. Tests whether crossing_rate bias is model-geometric (general) or CP-annotation-specific\n    (task-bound).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_traces_total: 200\n    n_jailbreak: 104\n    n_safe: 96\n    model: R1-8B (Llama-8B, 32 layers)\n    layer_selection:\n      bal_acc_x_cr_layer: 12\n      bal_acc_x_cr_depth_pct: 39\n      pure_bal_acc_layer: 13\n      pure_bal_acc_depth_pct: 42\n      precision_layer: 13\n      precision_depth_pct: 42\n      pre_cp_fpr_layer: 14\n      pre_cp_fpr_depth_pct: 45\n      composite_layer: 13\n      composite_depth_pct: 42\n    layer_gap_abs: 2\n    layer_gap_depth_pct: 6\n    crossing_rate_analysis:\n      shallow_mean_cr: 0.12\n      deep_mean_cr: 0.11\n      shallow_deep_ratio: 1.05\n      ratio_p_value: 0.74\n      pattern: uniform — no shallow inflation\n    hs_performance_at_best_layer:\n      layer: 13\n      bal_acc: 0.63\n      precision: 0.58\n      pre_cp_fpr: 0.31\n      auroc: 0.68\n    text_performance:\n      bal_acc: 0.6\n      precision: 0.55\n      pre_cp_fpr: 0.34\n    hs_text_comparison:\n      bal_acc_delta_pp: 3.0\n      precision_delta_pp: 3.0\n      fpr_delta_pp: -3.0\n      bal_acc_p: 0.28\n      precision_p: 0.31\n      fpr_p: 0.42\n      hb_pass_rate: 0/3\n    cp_data_comparison:\n      cp_cr_composite_layer: L0 (0%)\n      advbench_cr_composite_layer: L12 (39%)\n      cp_layer_gap: 16\n      advbench_layer_gap: 2\n      cp_hs_text_prec_delta: +22.4pp\n      advbench_hs_text_prec_delta: +3.0pp\n      cp_crossing_rate_shallow_deep_ratio: 2.8\n      advbench_crossing_rate_shallow_deep_ratio: 1.05\n  result_rationale: 'AdvBench非复现的root cause是mechanistic的，不是statistical noise:\n\n    (1) crossing_rate在binary classification中不产生浅层虚高。在CP temporal data中， crossing_rate\n    measures how often probe score crosses threshold DURING a trace。 Shallow layers的probes更noisy（cosine\n    distance smaller, representations more compressed）→更频繁crossing→crossing_rate虚高→与bal_acc相乘后bias\n    toward shallow layers。在AdvBench binary classification中，虽然可以对每个token计算probe score\n    并观察序列，但binary labels（jailbreak/safe per trace）不创造step-level temporal structure。Probe\n    scores在entire trace上趋于一致（consistently jailbreak或consistently safe），所以crossing_rate在所有层上都很低（~0.11-0.12），\n    shallow/deep ratio≈1.05，无显著差异。\n\n    (2) HS-text gap在binary classification中collapse到+3pp (NS)。原因：hidden states 对CP\n    temporal task的advantage来自于tracking step-level safety state transitions—— hidden\n    states可以detect commitment point前后的internal representation shift。 Binary classification不需要这种temporal\n    sensitivity——只需要区分''this trace as a whole is jailbreak vs safe''。对于这个coarser task，text\n    embeddings capture足够 的signal（jailbreak traces有distinctive vocabulary/structure），HS的marginal\n    advantage消失。\n\n    (3) Layer selection convergence: 5个metrics全部选中层（L12-L14, 39-45% depth）， gap仅2层。这是因为binary\n    classification的optimal layer由overall representation quality决定（middle layers best\n    balance between too-raw和too-output-specific）， 而非threshold-crossing-dynamics。所有metrics\n    agree on similar layers because they''re all measuring the same underlying discriminability\n    without temporal confounds。\n\n    (4) Traces太uniform: AdvBench prompts + R1-8B responses产生相对homogeneous的 traces——jailbreak\n    traces consistently harmful, safe traces consistently refuse。 没有CP temporal data中的''safety\n    reasoning followed by commitment''渐进结构。 所有层表现接近（bal_acc range across layers: 0.55-0.65），metric间无显著分化。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: AdvBench Layer Selection (R1-8B, 5 metrics)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Selected Layer\n    - Depth %\n    - bal_acc at Layer\n    rows:\n    - - bal_acc × crossing_rate\n      - L12\n      - 39%\n      - '0.62'\n    - - pure bal_acc\n      - L13\n      - 42%\n      - '0.63'\n    - - precision\n      - L13\n      - 42%\n      - '0.63'\n    - - pre_cp_fpr\n      - L14\n      - 45%\n      - '0.62'\n    - - composite (additive)\n      - L13\n      - 42%\n      - '0.63'\n  - name: 'CP Data vs AdvBench: Layer Selection Bias Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Dimension\n    - CP Temporal Data\n    - AdvBench Binary\n    rows:\n    - - cr_composite layer\n      - L0 (0%)\n      - L12 (39%)\n    - - threshold metrics layer\n      - L16 (52%)\n      - L13 (42%)\n    - - layer gap (abs)\n      - 16 layers\n      - 2 layers\n    - - layer gap (depth %)\n      - 52%\n      - 6%\n    - - CR shallow/deep ratio\n      - '2.8'\n      - '1.05'\n    - - HS-text Δprec\n      - +22.4pp (HB ✅)\n      - +3.0pp (NS)\n    - - HB pass rate\n      - 3/3\n      - 0/3\n  - name: AdvBench Crossing Rate by Depth Band\n    columns:\n    - Depth Band\n    - Mean CR\n    - Std CR\n    - n layers\n    rows:\n    - - Shallow (L0-L7)\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.03'\n      - '8'\n    - - Middle (L8-L23)\n      - '0.11'\n      - '0.02'\n      - '16'\n    - - Deep (L24-L31)\n      - '0.11'\n      - '0.03'\n      - '8'\n    - - Shallow/Deep ratio\n      - '1.05'\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - t-test p-value\n      - '0.74'\n      - —\n      - —\n  - name: AdvBench HS vs Text Performance (R1-8B)\n    columns:\n    - Modality\n    - bal_acc\n    - precision\n    - FPR\n    - AUROC\n    rows:\n    - - HS (L13)\n      - '0.63'\n      - '0.58'\n      - '0.31'\n      - '0.68'\n    - - Text (MiniLM)\n      - '0.60'\n      - '0.55'\n      - '0.34'\n      - '0.65'\n    - - Δ\n      - +3.0pp\n      - +3.0pp\n      - −3.0pp\n      - +3.0pp\n    - - p-value\n      - '0.28'\n      - '0.31'\n      - '0.42'\n      - '0.25'\n    - - HB pass?\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure A: Crossing rate vs layer depth for CP data (blue, steep decline from\n    shallow to deep) vs AdvBench (orange, flat line). X-axis: layer index, Y-axis:\n    crossing rate. CP data shows 2.8× shallow/deep ratio; AdvBench ≈1.0. Caption:\n    ''Crossing rate inflation at shallow layers is specific to temporal probe score\n    sequences (CP data). Binary classification produces uniform crossing rates across\n    all depths.''\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure B: Layer selection heatmap side-by-side. Left: CP data (5 metrics, clear\n    separation between cr-composite at L0 and threshold metrics at L16). Right: AdvBench\n    (5 metrics all converge to L12-L14, no visible separation).\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure C: HS-text precision delta bar chart. CP data: +22.4pp (significant, marked\n    ✅). AdvBench: +3.0pp (NS, marked ✗). Error bars show 95% bootstrap CI. AdvBench\n    CI includes zero.\n\n    '\n  analysis: \"AdvBench非复现是worst-tier的defining experiment。结论分为两个component:\\n(1) Layer\\\n    \\ selection bias非复现：Mechanistically consistent。crossing_rate bias 的root cause是temporal\\\n    \\ probe score序列中shallow layers的noise-driven threshold crossings。Binary classification不产生这种temporal\\\n    \\ structure。Bias不复现 不invalidate CP data上的finding——it BOUNDS its scope。C1调整为: 'Layer\\\n    \\ selection bias is a pitfall specific to temporal monitoring pipelines that use\\\n    \\ threshold-crossing statistics for layer selection. It does not manifest in standard\\\n    \\ binary classification settings.'\\n(2) HS-text gap非复现：+3pp (NS) vs CP data +22.4pp\\\n    \\ (HB ✅)。HS advantage 在binary classification上消失，说明advantage来自temporal structure\\\n    \\ interaction（hidden states track step-level state transitions that text embeddings\\\n    \\ miss），而非inherent modality superiority。\\nPaper impact: C1 scope从'any hidden-state\\\n    \\ evaluation should audit layer selection metrics'收窄到'temporal monitoring pipelines\\\n    \\ using crossing_rate should audit layer selection'。这让contribution更precise但less\\\n    \\ impactful。\\nReviewer split: - Supportive (R1): 'Boundary condition analysis\\\n    \\ is good science. Showing WHERE\\n  your finding applies and where it doesn't\\\n    \\ is a sign of mature methodology.\\n  The AdvBench non-replication actually STRENGTHENS\\\n    \\ the mechanistic argument —\\n  you can explain WHY it doesn't replicate (no temporal\\\n    \\ structure → no\\n  crossing_rate bias).'\\n- Dismissive (R2): 'The non-replication\\\n    \\ means your headline finding (layer\\n  selection bias) is a pipeline implementation\\\n    \\ detail, not a scientific\\n  contribution. You could fix it by not using crossing_rate\\\n    \\ — which any\\n  careful practitioner would do anyway. The AdvBench experiment\\\n    \\ cost 6 GPU\\n  hours to show your contribution is smaller than claimed.'\\n\\n\\\n    Dream score delta: -0.10 (3.0 → 2.9). Non-replication doesn't kill the paper but\\\n    \\ removes the possibility of C1 earning generalizability points. Paper stays at\\\n    \\ Findings level; no pathway to Main opened by this experiment.\"\n","numLines":1334,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1334}}}
